    <item>
      <title>Liverpool with Lauren Harris | Correspondent Week ep. 19 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>It's off to Merseyside for the final two Podcasts of Correspondent Week and on the penultimate episode of the week it's The Reds, now under Andon Iraola, and new Liverpool Correspondent Lauren Harris joins James to discuss the FPL assets of interest and what to expect next.

Maybe clean sheets aren't expected. But the case is put for and against investment and whether Virgil Van Dijk or Milos Kerkez should be preferred.

Alexander Isak is fit, maybe the answer to the Florian Wirtz or Domink Szoboszlai dilemma is to get both and there may be some cheaper options for consideration too.

But can Liverpool be successful with a renewed high energy game plan when the squad clearly needs reinforcements?



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 20 with Sean Norton on Everton




And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)




Next Week on Planet FPL:

Monday: s. 10 ep. 3 - The Shortlist

Tuesday: That Show With Nico ep. 16

Wednesday: s. 10 ep. 4 - The Line Ups

Thursday: Ask James

Friday: s. 10 ep. 5 - Final Drafts





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠







