    <item>
      <title>Arsenal with Adam Pritchard | Correspondent Week ep. 16 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>Day 4 of Correspondent Week concludes with Champions and title favourites Arsenal with Adam Pritchard joining James.

The Gunners open with Championship title winners Coventry City at The Emirates and therefore three FPL assets will be wanted by many FPL managers. But it's not straightforward.

Gabriel has had a big price hike to 8.0 and William Saliba is injured, so the door has opened to consider other Arsenal defenders and David Raya has been priced at 6.0.

Kai Havertz and Viktor Gyokeres are largely being overlooked due to a template front 3, and with the fitness of Bukayo Saka and Declan Rice remaining a concern new signings Christos Tzolis and Brino Guimaraes may be a route into Arsenal's attack.



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 17 with Andrew O'Gorman with Coventry City


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 17-20 with Andrew O'Gorman on Coventry, Simon Bibby on Newcastle, Lauren Harris on Liverpool and Sean Norton on Everton



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠







