      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>Day 4 of Correspondent Week concludes with Champions and title favourites Arsenal with Adam Pritchard joining James.</p>
<p>The Gunners open with Championship title winners Coventry City at The Emirates and therefore three FPL assets will be wanted by many FPL managers. But it's not straightforward.</p>
<p>Gabriel has had a big price hike to 8.0 and William Saliba is injured, so the door has opened to consider other Arsenal defenders and David Raya has been priced at 6.0.</p>
<p>Kai Havertz and Viktor Gyokeres are largely being overlooked due to a template front 3, and with the fitness of Bukayo Saka and Declan Rice remaining a concern new signings Christos Tzolis and Brino Guimaraes may be a route into Arsenal's attack.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 17 with Andrew O'Gorman with Coventry City</p>
<p>
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 17-20 with Andrew O'Gorman on Coventry, Simon Bibby on Newcastle, Lauren Harris on Liverpool and Sean Norton on Everton</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p>The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123">⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠</a></p>
