      <title>Bournemouth with Neil Grover | Correspondent Week ep. 15 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>A first ever European campaign is on the horizon for Bournemouth after they went the final half of last season without a singe defeat. But Andoni Iraola has moved on to Liverpool with Marco Rose is his replacement.

Bournemouth fan Neil Grover joins James to discuss what we can expect from Rose and The Cherries moving forward.

It's a difficult opening run of fixtures but plenty for FPL managers still to consider which features discussion on DEFCON defenders, new signings, Rayan, Marcus Tavernier and lots more.





Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 16 with Adam Pritchard on Arsenal


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 17-20 with Andrew O'Gorman on Coventry, Simon Bibby on Newcastle, Lauren Harris on Liverpool and Sean Norton on Everton



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠







