    <item>
      <title>Sunderland with Spencer Barrowman | Correspondent Week ep. 14 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>Most thought they wouldn't survive, but Sunderland caught everyone by surprise, perhaps even themselves, by qualifying for the Europa League. Now the excitement of European football awaits, but with it comes challenges. Do have Sunderland have the squad that cope with two games a week regularly?

That may take time to answer. But before European football begins there are some great opening fixtures and lots of FPL interest for fantasy managers to consider. 

Injury concerns have opened up the possibility of a 4.0 defender and a 4.5 OOP defender both starting and there's coverage of those who performed well last season too such as Dan Ballard and Nordi Mukiele.

And there are attackers too with 6.0 pair Enzo Le Fee and Brian Brobbey likely to have interest and there's someone cheaper who could catch the ere too.





Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 15 with Neil Grover on Bournemouth



And later on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week: ep. 16 with Adam Pritchard on Arsenal


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 17-20 with Andrew O'Gorman on Coventry, Simon Bibby on Newcastle, Lauren Harris on Liverpool and Sean Norton on Everton



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠







