    <item>
      <title>Ipswich Town with Paul Gaught-Allen | Correspondent Week ep. 13 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>The Tractor Boys are back, but it all feels a bit different. This time they may well be the promoted side expected to do best and they've got a new manager too in Gary O'Neil following the resignation of Kieran Mckenna. Can they upset the odds?

On the Pod, what to expect from O'Neil and assessment of all the FPL options with as as many as eight new signings potentially to start in GW1 (one hasn't signed yet!).

There appears to be clarity on who will start in goal, the best of the 4.0 defenders, midfield options and we may even have a 4.5 forward of genuine interest!



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 14 with Spencer Barrowman on Sunderland


And later today on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 15  &amp; 16 with Neil Grover on Bournemouth and Adam Pritchard on Arsenal



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





