    <item>
      <title>Crystal Palace with Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd | Correspondent Week ep. 12 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>James has been keenly looking forward to this one with the prospects of Crystal Palace assets potentially appealing for the long-term in FPL, but rumours of a move away for Daniel Munoz have thrown doubt into his mind, and there are further warmings from Palace fan Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd about their assets.

Lacroix has gone, as said Munoz may follow, could more leave? And what do Palace want to invest in?

There's coverage of several interesting FPL prospects including Dean Henderson, Chris Richards, Tyrick Mitchell, Isamaila Sarr and Jean-Philippe Mateta.

And an intro to new boss Pierre Sage who leads Palace into the Europa League and takes over from Oliver Glasner who has departed following the Conference League victory. 

 



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 13 with Paul Gaught-Allen on Ipswich


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 13-16 with Paul Gaught-Allen on Ipswich, Spencer Barrowman on Sunderland, Neil Grover on Bournemouth and Adam Pritchard on Arsenal



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠







