    <item>
      <title>Manchester City with Jonny Pringle | Correspondent Week ep. 11 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>It's the beginning on a new era at Manchester City with Pep Guardiola's 10 years of dominance coming to an end. His replacement is one of Pep's former assistants and the former Chelsea manager Enzo Maresca. Does it mean we can expect a continuation of what we've seen previously stylistically and tactically from City?

Jonny Pringle joins James to discuss the new era and all the potential FPL assets, featuring (of course) Erling Haaland, the attacking midfeld quartet of Rayan Cherki, Jeremy Doku, Phil Foden and Antoine Semenyo.

Plus, expectations for Elliot Anderson, if Rodri will leave and picking the best defensive asset looks tough with Nico O'Reilly, Marc Guehi and Josko Gvardiol all likely to be popular picks.



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 12 with Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd on Crystal Palace


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 13-16 with Paul Gaught-Allen on Ipswich, Spencer Barrowman on Sunderland, Neil Grover on Bournemouth and Adam Pritchard on Arsenal



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





