      <title>Tottenham with Ricky Saunders | Correspondent Week ep. 9 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>It was way too close for comfort last season for Tottenham. Surely it'll be better this time, won't it?

James is joined by fellow Tottenham fan Ricky Saunders to discuss excitement over an evolving football philosophy under Roberto De Zerbi and new signings in Jan Paul Van Hecke, Marcos Senesi, Andy Robertson, Sandro Tonali and Matheus Fernandes.

But there's concern, with no new forward additions and there may be only two fit forwards for three spots in Gameweek 1.

Plus FPL discussion on the Kinsky-Dubravka double up, best defensive assets, the cons to Richarlison or Solanke; but there may be one sneaky attacking asset worth an early punt.



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 10 with Tom Medd on Brentford


And later today on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 11 &amp; 12 with Jonny Pringle on Manchester City and Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd on Crystal Palace



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠⁠⁠







