      <itunes:summary>In the eyes of many neutrals Championship Play Off winners Hull City have got no chance. Some bad underlying numbers from last season, a thin and inexperience top level squad, injuries galore and a rough opening run of fixtures.

Yet all might not be how it appears on the surface. They are possibly about to go mental in the transfer window.

Danny MacDonald joins James to discuss all of The Tigers squad and there is clarity on who will start in goal, the prospects for talisman Oliver McBurnie and the 4.0 defenders and 4.5 midfielders who 'will' start in GW1.

And will uncertainty about how the squad will look in the near future how much should FPL managers target players against them?



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 8 with Lee Jackson on Aston Villa


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 9-12 with Ricky Saunders on Tottenham, Tom Medd on Brentford, Jonny Pringle on Manchester City and Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd on Crystal Palace



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠⁠⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠⁠⁠







