    <item>
      <title>Fulham with Lewis James | Correspondent Week ep. 5 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>Day 2 of Correspondent Week kicks off with a trip to The Cottage to talk all things Fulham with Lewis James as they begin a new era under manager Alvaro Arbeloa.

But there are some concerns from neutrals, with the experienced quartet of Issa Diop, Sasa Lukic, Harry Wilson and Raul Jimenez all leaving.

What can we expect from new signings Gonzalo Garcia and Cesar Palacios? Do they offer FPL appeal?

Plus, further FPL discussion on the defensive assets, if there's any gems in the midfield and awareness of three consecutive fixtures against the promoted sides, which comes at a period where many FPL managers may Wildcard. 



Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 6 with Ed Salinger on Leeds


Later today on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 6-8 with Ed Salinger on Leeds, Danny Macdonald on Hull and Lee Jackson on Aston Villa



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: ⁠https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123⁠







