    <item>
      <title>Manchester United with Alex Trembath | Correspondent Week ep. 4 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>Day 1 of Correspondent Week concludes with Manchester United fan Alex Trembath joining James to discuss The Red Devils and their FPL assets, and they start with games against two promoted clubs.

There's discussion on the importance of Bruno Fernandes for FPL managers and starting him with or instead of Erling Haaland, if there's a clear frontrunner in the Matheus Cunha or Bryan Mbeumo debate, managers may also want a defensive asset to start with too.

Plus, if we should expect more signings following the arrivals of Youri Tielemans and Andrey Santos, the future of Marcus Rashford and coverage of squad depth.




Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 5 with Lewis James on Fulham


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Correspondent Week episodes 5-8 with Lewis James on Fulham, Ed Salinger on Leeds, Danny Macdonald on Hull and Lee Jackson on Aston Villa



And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (BT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (IT+)





The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123







