    <item>
      <title>Nottingham Forest with Mark Sutherns | Correspondent Week ep. 2 | Planet FPL 2026/27</title>
      <description>Next up on Correspondent Week James is joined by Nottingham Forest fan Mark Sutherns to discuss Oliver Glasner replacing Vitor Pereira and all the Forest FPL assets ahead of the new season.

There's discussion on talisman Morgan Gibbs-White and if he is the right answer to the Cunha v Mbeumo debate, preferences between Nikola Milenkovic and Murillo, if Neco Williams is worth paying 0.5 more than Ola Aina and if Igor Jesus can keep up his positive pre season output to be an attractive buy at 6.0

Plus, the team looks quite settled for GW1 as it stands, but so far Forest have been quiet in the transfer window, and it might not stay that way. There's news of one new imminent arrival and there's likely to be more to arrive. Could Glasner go back to players he knows well at Palace!?







Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 3 with Gary Mantle on Chelsea

And later today: ep. 4 with Alex Trembath on Manchester United

And on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj and James on today's four Podcasts (BT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (IT+)



The full schedule for Correspondent Week can be found here: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/correspondent-166192123





