      <itunes:image href="https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/d4b668fc-8109-11f1-8efa-af2e4fb97147/image/f799871cfa3c53633a4b26e262520faf.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress"/>
      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>Everyone seems to know the score, they've seen it all before...

Suj and James discuss all The Fallout from England's World Cup Semi Final defeat to Argentina in Atlanta.

Where did it go so wrong after England went in front? An assessment of Thomas Tuchel's tactics and substitutions, whether the players on the pitch should take responsibility and Argentina's ability to throe caution to the wind, led by Lionel Messi.

And what lessons can be learned? Because so much of last night would have felt very familiar to many England fans.



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Weekender ep.43



Today on Patreon: Who Am I? World Cup Quiz (IT+) &amp; Talking Tottenham (AT)



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/content-schedule-163672783



