      <title>The Quarter Finals Review | Planet FPL 2026</title>
      <description>David and James discuss the weekend quarter finals, looking back at victories for Spain, England and Argentina that now sets up a mouthwatering semi final line up.

Spain now face France after another late Mikel Merino strike helped them overcome Belgium. Does it feel like the final before the final?

England and Argentina will hope not, but both needed extra time and Thomas Tuchel's words that England were 'lucky' are echoed on the Podcast, and Tuchel may reflect he too made some mistakes.

But England, and Jude Bellingham got the job done against Norway and now meet old rivals Argentina who beat Switzerland after Breel Embolo's red card impacted a previously close encounter.

Will there be changes to the starting line-up and might Argentina change system?

 



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: That Show With Nico ep.14



Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+) &amp; Talking Tactics (IT+)



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/content-schedule-163672783





