      <itunes:image href="https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/99de734e-7acb-11f1-b015-3357dbef5b59/image/6977994d6e0ab73370d55aa65c25cac4.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress"/>
      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>David and James discuss key moments and thoughts from the 8 ties in the Last 16 and the four teams kept apart in each quarter of the draw could yet make up a dream semi final line-up. But World Champions Argentina were given an almighty scare by Egypt yesterday and their come from behind victory wasn't without controversy.

And there was plenty of controversy in the build up to the USA's game on Monday night, but Belgium put on their best display to date to romp away with it in Seattle. They will meet Spain next after the saw off Portugal through an injury time Mikel Merino goal.

France and Morocco will meet after they both won on Saturday, we had to wait for penalties for drama as Switzerland beat Colombia and Erling Haaland scored both as Norway beat a Brazil side who now may feel the have a curse when meeting European opponents.

And the Podcast concludes with a bit of FIFA Fantasy chat ahead of the Quarters. 

 



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James, scheduled for 12pm BST with an audio podcast to follow shortly after conclusion



Today on Patreon: Tot &amp; Ham (IT+) &amp; On This Day: Brazil 1-7 Germany (IT+) 



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/content-schedule-163031086






