      <itunes:author>Suj &amp; James</itunes:author>
      <itunes:image href="https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/fc00245c-7916-11f1-828d-ffbfc3a69dd4/image/8646984b23faa46a22fabafc8810e2d7.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress"/>
      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>An England victory that will never be forgotten. 3-2 winners in the Azteca against Mexico despite playing the majority of the second half with ten men - and now the excitement will really build.

David and James are still up having not slept since full time and discuss all the key talking points from a tie that began with kick off shenanigans, and ended with a freak injury.

In between Jude Bellingham delivered, Anthony Gordon impressed, there were three big refereeing decisions and The Three Lions fought like heroes to get over the line.

This was a night (and morning!) to celebrate for England fans, but there is still much to improve on. There's discussion on a shift in some of Thomas Tuchel's tactics and a look ahead to Saturday's Quarter Final against Erling Haaland's Norway.





Tomorrow on Planet FPL: That Show With Nico ep.13



Today on Patreon: How Old Is He? Quiz (AT &amp; IT+) &amp; The Monday Night Watchalong, Spain v Portugal with James (Available to all Patreon members)



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/content-schedule-163031086





