    <item>
      <title>The Fallout: England 2-1 DR Congo | Planet FPL 2026</title>
      <description>It can't ever just be easy can it?

Suj and James discuss England's victory in Atlanta  against DR Congo as Harry Kane's brace sealed The Three Lions first victory at a World Cup after conceding first since 1966.

Discussion features key moments from the game, Kane's brilliance, how DR Congo's brave tactics confused England, the continuation of England's problems in the wide positions, and the options at right-back.

Next, it's Mexico in the Azteca for The Three Lions and a very real serious test of England's credentials. 





Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Weekender ep.41



Today on Patreon: Money in Football (IT+)



