      <itunes:image href="https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/c4f64882-7467-11f1-af4d-37ca05339642/image/7986fbc9e48132afd1d685a7234e5c56.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress"/>
      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>A relaxed chat with Nico and James about some hot topics at the World Cup including last night's penalty shoot out defeats for Germany and The Netherlands.

On the Podcast, Germany were bad (and have been bad for a while); Morocco well deserved to go through after The Dutch changed system; Brazil got it done against Japan; Nico is not happy with Portugal but has hopes Cape Verde can cause another shock.

Plus, Uruguay's unhappy exit; will FIFA be disappointed there hasn't been many meetings at the tournament between the traditional big nations; Assim Madibo's five game ban; would England losing tomorrow be their worst ever World Cup result; Djed Spence blanking Thomas Partey; there's a forward who thinks he could be as good as the elite





Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James, live stream scheduled for 12pm BST with an audio Podcast posted shortly after conclusion



Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+) &amp; Highlights from last night's Brazil-Japan Watchalong (AT)



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/content-schedule-162372704





