        <![CDATA[<p>A relaxed chat with Nico and James about some hot topics at the World Cup including last night's penalty shoot out defeats for Germany and The Netherlands.</p>
<p>On the Podcast, Germany were bad (and have been bad for a while); Morocco well deserved to go through after The Dutch changed system; Brazil got it done against Japan; Nico is not happy with Portugal but has hopes Cape Verde can cause another shock.</p>
<p>Plus, Uruguay's unhappy exit; will FIFA be disappointed there hasn't been many meetings at the tournament between the traditional big nations; Assim Madibo's five game ban; would England losing tomorrow be their worst ever World Cup result; Djed Spence blanking Thomas Partey; there's a forward who thinks he could be as good as the elite</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James, live stream scheduled for 12pm BST with an audio Podcast posted shortly after conclusion</p>
