    <item>
      <title>The MD3 Weekend Review | Planet FPL 2026</title>
      <description>David and James discuss all the football played at the World Cup since Friday as the Group Stages came to an end.

Discussion features a Ousmane Dembele hat-trick, Senegal's five star win saw them through as the worst best third placed team, Spain saw off Uruguay and there was carnage in Kansas as Austria and Algeria (sort of) played out a draw that suited both.

Colombia's point saw them finish about opponents Portugal, Belgium impressed, Iran were unlucky and the draw has opened up for Argentina to do well.

And England will now face DR Congo following Saturday's win against Panama.

 



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: That Show With Nico ep. 12



Today on Patreon: The Monday Night Watchalong, Brazil v Japan from 545pm BST with James (Available to all Patrons including free members) &amp; a Quiz on England in major tournament knockout matches (IT+)



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl/posts/content-schedule-162372704





