      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>David and James complete their trilogy of World Cup and FIFA Fantasy previews today by looking at Groups I-L.</p>
<p>And there are some heavy hitters in this preview with four of the top six in the betting for the tournament covered, with France, Argentina, Portugal and England all fancied to win their groups.</p>
<p>But there are threats, with Colombia, Norway and Senegal tipped to do well and England will be challenged by old foes Croatia.</p>
<p>All the big hitting Fantasy forwards feature here with Haaland, Kane, Mabppe, Messi, Ronaldo and covered, but there are some differentials and enabliong players for Fantasy managers to consider too.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: World Cup Final Thoughts with James</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Today on Patreon: FPL At World Cups Quiz with Gary Robinson (IT+)</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>

The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-160494552





</p>
