    <item>
      <title>Reintroducing Ipswich | The Fan View with Paul Gaught-Allen | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>At the first time of asking Ipswich Town have returned to the Premier League and will hope to improve on their showing two seasons ago that followed unexpected back to back promotions.

But something doesn't feel right. 

James is joined by Ipswich fan Paul Gaught-Allen to discuss what's changed at Ipswich over the last 12 months,

The exciting football from the 2024 promotion has given way to something that some would say isn't as beautiful on the eye. Success this past season was in Paul's own words, something that felt more 'transactional'. 

But does that mean Ipswich have learned lessons and are now better equipped to stay up this time?



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Weekender ep.37



Today on Patreon: Money in Football (IT+) &amp; Memories of '94: The European Underdogs (AT)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/159799268






