    <item>
      <title>Man Utd v Nott'm Forest | CotC with Alex Trembath &amp; Mark Sutherns | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Manchester United fan Alex Trembath and Nottingham Forest fan Mark Sutherns to discuss the latest at their clubs, but with objectives achieved are both teams now 'on the beach?' And is that good or bad for FPL managers?

United will back in the Champions League next season and almost certain to finish third, with rumours now suggesting Michael Carrick will get the job permanently. Is that right? And how much does the club need to invest in the transfer window?

Forest have been on a great run under Vitor Pereira and are now clear from relegation fears, but there was big disappointment in the Europa League semi final defeat to Aston Villa. What's next for Forest and Pereira?

Plus, FPL discussion includes a look at one and two week punts, end of season motivation, Morgan Gibbs-White's form and whether Bruno Fernandes is the go-to captain for GW37.





Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James, live stream scheduled for 1230pm with an audio Podcast of the stream posted shortly after conclusion



Today on Patreon: Money in Football (IT+) &amp; What The Numbers Say (IT+)



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/posts/157921345








