    <item>
      <title>Double Trouble | Planet FPL S. 9 Ep. 52 | GW35 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>A dramatic weekend in the Premier League reviewed with Suj and James as the race for the title and the battle to stay up took major twists and there are potentially big implications for Fantasy managers as a result.

Arsenal won comfortably but Manchester City escaped from Everton with a draw giving Arsenal a big advantage in the race for the title. Win at West Ham and it looks to be theirs, but The Hammers will be desperate having fallen a point behind Tottenham in the race for 17th,.

That race to stay up is now almost certainly a two-way battle as Tottenham deserved won against a woeful Aston Villa, whilst Leeds won and so to did Nottingham Forest despite fielding an under strength team against a Chelsea who did at least finally score but were again very bad.

And Bournemouth now lead the way ahead of Brentford for 6th which could yet result in qualification for The Champions League.

Eyes now are on Arsenal assets and also Manchester City and Crystal Palace ahead of the Double Gameweek. 

But James also has two other teams on mind for investment despite neither team winning this weekend and there is deliberation as to whether Palace should be invested in at all.

And there is a big warning about the rotation headaches that may hit Fantasy managers hard, and not just this coming Gameweek.





Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Manchester City v Crystal Palace with Jonny Pringle &amp; Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd



Today on Patreon: UCL Fantasy Preview (IT+)  Away Days: Aston Villa (IT+)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/posts/157375940







