      <itunes:image href="https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/0d3f6b9a-4476-11f1-9170-f3ec5049672c/image/20c238845675e0237acb392fa8b802d7.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress"/>
      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>One is bottom and just lost to a team that hasn't won in four months, the other was just beaten 5-0 at home.

On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Wolves fan Bradley Parker and Sunderland fan Spencer Barrowman to discuss the mood at their clubs ahead of Saturday's meeting at Molineux.

Wolves relegation has been inevitable but a late
winter/early Spring upturn in form and results has been followed by three
consecutive defeats without scoring against teams placed 15th, 17th and 18th in the table. What's happened to the positivity prior to the International break?

The team in 16th just trounced Sunderland at The Stadium of Light 5-0, which followed on from conceding four at Villa Park, when they also were on a positive run previously.

There's discussion one hat remains and early thoughts on next season, including whether the managers will still be there.

Plus, FPL discussion on enablers that perhaps shouldn't necessarily be overlooked. Especially, as they're playing each other.



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Weekender ep.32



Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ham (IT+) &amp; Talking Tactics (AT)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/posts/156649918









