      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>David joins James for a discussion on the four games that concluded Double Gameweek 33 as West Ham earned a point at Crystal Palace, Brighton cut a woeful Chelsea apart that led to the dismissal of Liam Rosenior, Bournemouth and Leeds shared four goals and Manchester City went top but only got the one through Erling Haaland at Turf Moor.

There's discussion on what may happen with the yet to be arranged Manchester City and Crystal Palace fixture and a flavour of what David and James do on The Weekender with a look at Free Hit and Wildcard Drafts for the upcoming Blank Gameweek 34.



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, West Ham v Everton with Chris Stone &amp; Sean Norton



Today on Patreon: Money in Football (IT+)  &amp; The Midweek FPL Dilemma (AT)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-april-156064381






