    <item>
      <title>Lose One's Temper | Planet FPL S. 9 Ep. 49 | GW33 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>On the review of the Double Gameweek weekend it's been a good weekend for many engaged managers on bench boost and that includes Suj despite buying a player who didn't even show up at the weekend, whilst for those likes James who have gone against it's been a case of trying to survive.

All the games reviewed including Manchester City's victory against Arsenal which leaves us with an exciting title run-in, Liverpool stole the Merseyside Derby late on, whilst there was also late heartbreak for Tottenham against Brighton and Chelsea's woes continued as they were beaten by Manchester United.

Focus now turns away from those who doubled to those who didn't ahead of the Gameweek 34 Blank and there were a number of haulers with a single who may now be popular such as Ollie Watkins and Morgan Gibbs-White and the FPL teams who look strongest this coming week are likely to have a lot of red in them.



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Manchester United v Brentford with Alex Trembath &amp; Tom Medd



Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+)  &amp; Slack Stories (AT)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-april-156064381





