      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>On the review of the Double Gameweek weekend it's been a good weekend for many engaged managers on bench boost and that includes Suj despite buying a player who didn't even show up at the weekend, whilst for those likes James who have gone against it's been a case of trying to survive.</p>
<p>All the games reviewed including Manchester City's victory against Arsenal which leaves us with an exciting title run-in, Liverpool stole the Merseyside Derby late on, whilst there was also late heartbreak for Tottenham against Brighton and Chelsea's woes continued as they were beaten by Manchester United.</p>
<p>Focus now turns away from those who doubled to those who didn't ahead of the Gameweek 34 Blank and there were a number of haulers with a single who may now be popular such as Ollie Watkins and Morgan Gibbs-White and the FPL teams who look strongest this coming week are likely to have a lot of red in them.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Manchester United v Brentford with Alex Trembath &amp; Tom Medd</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+)  &amp; Slack Stories (AT)</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>

The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-april-156064381



</p>
