        <![CDATA[<p>A week of swings in FPL with the Wildcard to Bench Boost crowd going against everyone else, and ultimately many did quite similar. But that won't be the case everywhere...</p>
<p>Suj and James discuss all the key talking points and games from the weekend as Jarrod Bowen and Igor Thiago rewarded those who held or invested, but there were others with doubles to come who performed well such as Bart Verbruggen and Neco O'Reilly. But O'Reilly may now be out so is it now a case of Marc Guehi versus Rayan Cherki for the third City spot in the double? Can managers dare to take Erling Haaland or Antoine Semenyo on?</p>
<p>Coverage of the teams who double, which includes a Bournemouth side who blew the title race back open with a brilliant victory at Arsenal, which means City could be top in 9 days.</p>
<p>Plus, why different strategies for 33 may alter the players that are of interest and Tottenham have entered the bottom three. </p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Bournemouth v Leeds United with Neil Grover &amp; Ed Salinger</p>
