      <itunes:image href="https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/d0c75a40-3275-11f1-9bf2-cbb41a13e0b5/image/813f01bd070ed4fec6d714c2471ef6c8.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress"/>
      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>It was all looking so straightforward for those intending to Wildcard in GW32 and Bench Boost in GW33, but then Southampton beat Arsenal in a Saturday night FA Cup shocker - and then there was the drama of Leeds beating West Ham on penalties that might hinder strategists too.

So what now for Chip Strategy? David joins James for a detailed discussion and a look at the different paths managers can take for the FPL run-in, including the big predicament facing many Wildcarders. Should they really make their GW32 team look worse to get a better GW33 Bench Boost!?

Alternatives for those with all chips intact are covered, and we've not forgotten those who are short of chips either.

There's focus on Wildcard 32v35 and why the right answer for some might be neither, free hit 33v34, what's likely to happen with the still unarranged Manchester City versus Crystal Palace fixture, Bench Boost opportunities and concerns plus lots more...



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: That Show With Nico ep.7



Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+) &amp; Nico's Corner (AT)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/154986197




