        <![CDATA[<p>Another horror weekend for Tottenham features heavily on the Gameweek Review Podcast as they lost the big 6 pointer against Nottingham Forest, meaning there could be another change of manager in the offing shortly.</p>
<p>The only good news was West Ham lost too, and there were others higher up the league who will be feeling particularly disgruntled, with Newcastle losing the Tyne-Wear Derby despite taking an early lead and Chelsea were taken apart at Everton.</p>
<p>And for FPL managers it's a time for calm with the Gameweek 32 deadline 18 days away and the FA Cup Quarter Finals likely to prove pivotal to strategy.</p>
<p>But there's still plenty to speculate on and one of the teams who could suddenly become of serious interest is Brighton.</p>
