    <item>
      <title>Bad Bench Good Boost | Planet FPL S. 9 Ep. 42 | GW28 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>It was an unforgettable week for many FPL managers, and that included James, whose bench boost went bust with three no shows, but a score of 99 still meant a big jump inside the top 10k.

For Suj it was a bit more forgettable. Infact, the only good news was a defeat for Nottingham Forest at Brighton, as Suj's West Ham and James' Tottenham once again fell to defeats. 

Those defeats feature in a review of all the games from a weekend that featured high drama, many popular FPL assets returning big, others including Erling Haaland no showing and now many are faced with multiple flags in their team, at a period where many may have wanted to roll transfers.

So now what ahead of the quick turnaround before GW29!?



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Newcastle United v Manchester United with Simon Bibby &amp; Alex Trembath



Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+) &amp; Away Days: Fulham (AT)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: 
https://www.patreon.com/posts/152025808






