    <item>
      <title>Planning A GW24 Wildcard? | Chip Talk | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>Why Wildcard now? For Suj and James, their strategy will likely be to wait for Gameweek 32 ahead of doubles and blanks, but there are plenty who are going now.

Suj and James explore why many are making the decision to Wildcard now, including teams that could have assets that are desirable, and assets that may be binned.

And very importantly there's a look at strategy ideas for those on Wildcard, including understanding future fixture swings, the impact on Chip usage, including if it means a bench boost should be used soon, how to mask potential deficiencies for DGW33, squad depth, managing BGW31, the importance of rolling transfers and a look at a possible draft.



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Chelsea v West Ham United with Gary Mantle &amp; Chris Stone



Today on Patreon: Tot &amp; Ham (IT+) &amp; Away Days: Burnley 24/1/26 (AT)





The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/149143462






