      <title>Wolves v Newcastle | CotC with Bradley Parker &amp; Simon Bibby | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Wolves fan Bradley Parker and Newcastle fan Simon Bibby to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Sunday's meeting at Molineux.

Both have hit a recent resurgence of form when it was really needed, with both unbeaten in four in all competitions, with Newcastle winning their last three in the Premier League and Wolvescfinally managed their first league win of the season against West Ham. Cause for optimism or do respective concerns persist for both?

Matheus Mane, price as a 4.5 forward in FPL is now attracting serious attention and looks good for minutes moving forward. But is he the only Wolves asset that can be considered.

Bruno Guimaraes is having an outstanding season, but is there a case to now ignore him and the likes of Malick Thiaw and Anthony Gordon as Newcastle approach a difficult and packed schedule starting with tonight's Carabao Cup Semi Final 1st leg against Manchester City?



Follow Bradley on Twitter/x: https://x.com/parker_bradley

Follow Si on Twitter/x: https://x.com/fplbibs



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James, live stream scheduled for 1230pm GMT with an audio to follow shortly after conclusion.



Today on Patreon: Champions League Winners Quiz with James Johnson (IT+) &amp; What The Numbers Say (AT) 







The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/148018953








