      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Wolves fan Bradley Parker and Newcastle fan Simon Bibby to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Sunday's meeting at Molineux.</p>
<p>Both have hit a recent resurgence of form when it was really needed, with both unbeaten in four in all competitions, with Newcastle winning their last three in the Premier League and Wolvescfinally managed their first league win of the season against West Ham. Cause for optimism or do respective concerns persist for both?</p>
<p>Matheus Mane, price as a 4.5 forward in FPL is now attracting serious attention and looks good for minutes moving forward. But is he the only Wolves asset that can be considered.</p>
<p>Bruno Guimaraes is having an outstanding season, but is there a case to now ignore him and the likes of Malick Thiaw and Anthony Gordon as Newcastle approach a difficult and packed schedule starting with tonight's Carabao Cup Semi Final 1st leg against Manchester City?</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Follow Bradley on Twitter/x: https://x.com/parker_bradley</p>
<p>Follow Si on Twitter/x: https://x.com/fplbibs</p>
