      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Nottingham Forest fan Mark Sutherns and Chelsea fan Gary Mantle to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Saturday's lunchtime meeting between the two clubs at The City Ground.</p>
<p>Ange Postecoglu is still Forest manager despite speculation he may be removed having won none of his seven games in charge and with many Forest fans not taking to the former Tottenham manager. Does Ange deserve more time? Or is the writing already on the wall?</p>
<p>Chelsea's Enzo Maresca was also facing scrutiny but the late GW7 victory against Liverpool has lifted the move. With brilliant fixtures ahead can The Blues get themselves into contention for the title?</p>
<p>Plus, all they key FPL discussion on Chelsea features defensive assets, Enzo Fernandez and Joao Pedro, whilst Forest assets have got to be cut it feels, but maybe with one exception.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Follow Mark on Twitter/x: https://x.com/FFScout_Mark</p>
<p>Follow Gary on Twitter/x: https://x.com/Phantomantle</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Weekender with David &amp; James</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Today on Patreon: Money in Football (IT+) &amp; Best Eleven: Monaco (AT)




The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/141099507


</p>
<p><br></p>
