    <item>
      <title>A Defensive Conclusion | Planet FPL S. 9 Ep. 18 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James take the opportunity of the second International break to discuss learnings from the small sample of data learnings from the season so far with conversation featuring DEFCONs, talismen, over and underperformers.

Defensive contributions (DEFCONs) is still in its infancy of many FPL managers mind and there's a look at teams DEFCONs accumulations for and against plus discussion on best individuals so far and moving forward. There's also a specific focus on clearances achieved as a strong metric to consider when looking for defenders who may achieve DEFCON and there's spmething very interesting in individuals year on year comparison.

Plus, the search for talismen is on, though currently they appear hard to find as many attacking assets have frustrated so far.

There's also a look at those who have over and underperformed in front of goal so far and a look at the next five fixtures for those who may want to Wildcard now... and there's also a look at GWs 13-17 for those who are holding on for later.



