<p>Liverpool lost again with another blank for Mohamed Salah in their late defeat at Chelsea which means Arsenal, victors against Suj's West Ham, are now top, but it was a disappointing day for Viktor Gyokeres owners.</p>
<p>James' Tottenham are now third but the result was again better than the display in victory at Leeds where Mohammed Kudus starred and returned well.</p>
<p>All the games reviewed with eyes on moves for after the International break. Who's on radar? Who's for the chop? And there's a warning that a number of FPL forwards may be about to do well in forthcoming weeks.</p>
