<p>Suj and James try to make some sense of the noise as they review all the games from Gameweek 3, which included brilliant away wins for Bournemouth and Crystal Palace, Manchester United leaving it late at Old Trafford against Burnley, Manchester City slipping up again at Brighton and Liverpool beating Arsenal at Anfield.</p>
<p>There's tips for those on Wildcard and Free Hit ahead of Gameweek 4, players under consideration for purchase and sale and tactical notes from the weekend which included West Ham's switch to a back four in victory at Nottingham Forest and Newcastle's surprise selections in their bore draw at Leeds.</p>
