    <item>
      <title>The Jury's Out | Planet FPL S. 9 Ep. 11 | GW2 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James review another dramatic weekend for FPL managers, with more popular assets blanking and some others now injured. It means for many action needs to be taken, but there's a key reminder on this Podcast of one very big reason why patience may be the right play for many.

All the games reviewed, which featured another humbling for West Ham where Joao Pedro went big, Tottenham putting in a professional display at Manchester City and earning a deserved victory, Arsenal got five against Leeds, there were important wins for Brentford and Burnley and Liverpool won at Newcastle last night in dramatic fashion.

Transfer targets are a theme of the Podcast, particularly in the midfield area and there's a warning to consider the unknowns when thinking about many players of interest.



Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream, at a to be confirmed time.



Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A (IT+) &amp; Away Days: Manchester City (IT+)



The full Planet FPL schedule for this week can be found via this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-137364856



