    <item>
      <title>Aston Villa with Lee Jackson | Correspondent Week ep.16 | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>Lee Jackson joins James on the conclusion of Day 4 to discuss all things Aston Villa, and the recording comes hot after Morgan Rogers limped off only seven minutes into his appearance for Aston Villa last night.

There's discussion on Villa with and without Rogers, and what it might mean for talisman Ollie Watkins ahead of the opener against Newcastle and a very appealing opening seven fixtures.

Donyell Malen was catching the attention of the FPL community even before the Rogers injury scare, his prospects, the fellow 5.5 midfielders and the slightly more expensive Youri Tielemans are assessed.

And Villa did start keeping clean sheets towards the end of the season. With those brilliant fixtures in mind is there a 4.5 gem to be considered?

Follow Lee on on Twitter/x: https://x.com/Lee_Jackson_92

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.17 with Adam Pritchard on Arsenal

Tomorrow on Correspondent Week: Adam Pritchard on Arsenal, Sam Murray on Brighton, Ricky Saunders on Tottenham Hotspur and Spencer Barrowman on Sunderland

