      <title>Chelsea with Gary Mantle | Correspondent Week ep.12 | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>Day 3 of Correspondent Week concludes with Gary Mantle joining James to talk all things Chelsea including all the summer incomings and outgoings.

One of those who has arrived is Joao Pedro has starred at the Club World Cup, but many are bemused by his current 50%+ ownership in FPL, though Gary thinks that at 7.5 he may well be underpriced!

He's not the only Blues asset with high ownership with Cole Palmer likely to be a lock for many FPL managers for GW1.

There's also conversation on defensive assets including Robert Sanchez, Marc Cucurella and Levi Colwill, Alternative attacking assets such as Pedro Neto and Enzo Fernandez are debated and could Moises Caicedo be the standout 5.5?

Plus, there's thoughts on what could yet happen in the transfer market and how some who are leaving the club but staying in the Premier League could do for FPL.



Follow Gary on on Twitter/x: https://x.com/Phantomantle

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.13 with Jonny Pringle on Manchester City

Tomorrow on Correspondent Week: Jonny Pringle on Manchester City, Sean Norton on Everton, Bradley Parker on Wolves and Lee Jackson on Aston Villa

Tonight on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)



