      <itunes:subtitle></itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>It's been a summer of frustration for many Newcastle fans, with only Anthony Elanga signed, depth not yet added in key positions and now star striker Alexander Isak is said to want out.

Simon Bibby joins James to try and make sense of what's happening with Isak and Newcastle's possible efforts to replace him.

There's discussion on new signing Elanga, and fellow attacking midfielders that may even include Anthony Gordon starting as a central forward.

There's coverage of the defensive assets and the fixture swings that will create interest... but should we just ignore for FPL for now?

Follow Si on Twitter/x: https://x.com/fplBibs

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.12 with Gary Mantle on Chelsea

Tomorrow on Correspondent Week: Jonny Pringle on Manchester City, Sean Norton on Everton, Bradley Parker on Wolves and Lee Jackson on Aston Villa

Tonight on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)



