    <item>
      <title>Bournemouth with Neil Grover | Correspondent Week ep.7 | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>They've had their defence ripped from them with Milos Kerkez and Dean Huijsen gone, and Ilia Zabarnyi set to follow, so how concerned should we be about Bournemouth ahead of their opening night trip to Anfield?

Neil Grover joins James to discuss what may be a makeshidt backline that starts the season, but it doesn't mean there isn't reason for optimism.

The attacking players have stayed and there's coverage of Antoine Semenyo, Justin Kluivert and Evanilson who are likely to attract particular interest for those Free Hitting in GW2.

And despite the issues there are defensive assets and midfield enablers worth considering too.



Follow Neil on Twitter/x: https://x.com/AFCBNG

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.8 with Tom Medd on Brentford

Tomorrow on Correspondent Week: Chris Stone on West Ham, Alex Trembath on Manchester United, Simon Bibby on Newcastle and Gary Mantle on Chelsea

Tonight on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)



