    <item>
      <title>Fulham with Lewis James | Correspondent Week ep.6 | Planet FPL 2025/26</title>
      <description>Next up on Correspondent Week James is joined by Fulham fan Lewis James to discuss The Cottagers and ask why everything feels so quiet on the transfer front and is it causing concern?

What it does mean currently is that Fulham have stability and there are some very interesting FPL assets up for discussion with the likes of Rodrigo Muniz potentially underpriced, and there's a clear standout from the defensive options with concerns around the fitness of Antonee Robinson.

And there are two midfielders under real consideration for Lewis to start with in his team, and one of them, you may have never heard of!



Follow Lewis on Twitter/x: https://x.com/LewisFFCJames

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.7 with Neil Grover on Bournemouth

Later today on Correspondent Week: Tom Medd on Brentford

Tonight on Patreon: The Debrief with Suj on today's four Podcasts (IT+) and After The Podcast with today's Correspondents (AT)



