    <item>
      <title>The Deals So Far | The Transfer Window Show | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss the latest transfers news following the closure of yesterday's first summer transfer window, the mini window, designed for players to be signed for the Club World Cup, so there's particular focus on the deals by Chelsea and Manchester City ahead of that tournament.

There's a look at interest in Bournemouth's brightest talents, Liverpool's move for Florian Wirtz, the keeper change at Brentford, links with Bryan Mbeumo to Tottenham and Manchester United, how Matheus Cunha may fit in at Old Trafford, Arsenal's likely striker transfer choice and more.


Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Club World Cup Preview



Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ham (IT+) and The Midweek FPL Dilemma assessing the prospect of a GW1 Bench Boost (IT+)



For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-131020394



Want to become a member of our FPL community and support the Podcast? 



