    <item>
      <title>He Told No Lies | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 52 | GW37 Review Part 2 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>James is back from Bilbao and victorious, to join Suj and discuss the final 3 games of Gameweek 37 which saw 15 goals scored including a goal of the season contender and Omar Marmoush and Ebe Eze scored late despite being named as a substitute.

There's thoughts on Sunday's final day with thoughts on players to purchase, what Free Hitters may want to consider, Assman selections and who will clinch those crucial Champions League places.

And the Podcast concludes with discussion on Wednesday's Europa League Final where Tottenham ended a 17 year trophy drought by beating Manchester United.



Tomorrow on on Planet FPL: The Fan View with Gary Mantle on Chelsea's bid for Champions League qualification and their upcoming Conference League Final



Today on Patreon: The Differential Show (IT+)  &amp; Away Days: The Europa League Final 2025 (IT+)


For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/129222338



