    <item>
      <title>Too Long; Didn't Read | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 50 | GW36 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Clayton joins James this week on the Gameweek Review Podcast to discuss all the weekend's games, which included more misfiring premiums, but there were good returns to be had elsewhere and that included a haul for Ebe Eze against a hapless and rotated Tottenham.

For Tottenham and Manchester United (who were beaten by West Ham) all focus is on the Europa League Final which is why Ollie Watkins and Cole Palmer are likely to be so popular this week for Fantasy managers! Should they be under captaincy consideration?

Plus, Arsenal pulled it back at Anfield where Trent Alexander-Arnold was booed, Newcastle beat 10 man Chelsea who saw Nicolas Jackson sent off, Villa, Brentford and Brighton picked up important wins, whilst Forest slipped up against Leicester and Southampton somehow held Manchester City and a returning Erling Haaland to claw themselves to 12 points.

Fantasy targets for what remains covered, the pull of rolling for GW38, what will Palace and City do next week following the FA Cup Final, players to consider for those with a Free Hit left and lots more... 



Tomorrow on on Planet FPL: The Clayton &amp; James Show



Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+) &amp; Nico's Corner (AT)



For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/128737590



Want to become a member of our FPL community and support the Podcast? 



