    <item>
      <title>Fill In The Blanks | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 47 | GW33 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss the 10 games played so far in Double Gameweek 33 where despite ther teams doubling scoring twelve and conceding only once it felt like the majority of FPL managers missed those who hauled.

There's a heavy focus on looking ahead with the Blank Gameweek next, with advice for those on Free Hit, those buying to keep and hold and which assets should be sacrificed who have just had doubles.

Captaincy is covered with a clear stand out (spoiler: it won't surprise), and there's particular focus on Fulham, Newcastle and Wolves assets as they get set to face the bottom three.

All the games covered with thoughts on Pep's latest tactical tweak as Man City left it late against Everton, how rampant Aston Villa saw off Newcastle and there was important victories too for Brentford and Forest in their bid to reach Europe; and both of those clubs will featuring heavily in the minds of Fantasy managers in the weeks to come, despite them meeting each other next. 

Tomorrow on on Planet FPL: The Clayton &amp; James Show

Today on Patreon: The Patreon QNA (IT+)

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-127192113

Want to become a member of our FPL community and support the Podcast? 

