    <item>
      <title>A Free Hit &amp; Something Quite... | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 41 | GW29 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James review the Blank Gameweek of 29 and very differing FPL fortunes as Suj's Free Hit went from a dreadful Saturday to a spectacular Sunday, whilst James' weekend was without a Free Hit and instead something altogether ****!

...And that's before conversation gets to Tottenham's latest defeat!

All games covered including Bruno Fernandes' haul in Manchester United's victory at woeful Leicester, it was Anthony Elanga rather than Chris Wood who went big as Forest also won well on the road, Brighton were unfortunate not to take all 3 points from Manchester City and Brentford produced perhasp the surprise of the weekend, with victory at Bournemouth.

It's over two weeks until GW30 and there's a repeat of how information will be king going into the next Gameweek, there's discussion on players of interest, targeting the bottom 3, points chasing, Erling Haaland and more...

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Fan View, with Newcastle United correspondent Simon Bibby

Today on Patreon: The Q'N'A (IT+), Nico's Corner (AT) and Away Days: Fulham (At)

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-124540484

