    <item>
      <title>Ask James | Friday January 31st | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>James' live stream is dominated with Chip questions following the Premier League's shock announcement today that the GW29 fixtures of Arsenal v Chelsea, Aston Villa v Liverpool and Fulham v Tottenham will be brought forward to GW25 in the event that they need to be postponed to accommodate a team playing in the Carabao Cup Final.

James explains the possibilities and why this announcement could have a huge bearing on the future Double Gameweeks of 33 and 36.

Plus, should those intending to Triple Captain Mo Salah now abort and play the Assistant Manager Chip instead? And if the do, should it be on Arne Slot or David Moyes?

Plus, why possible Gameweek 25 doublers should be held, why it may now pay to wait on Bournemouth and Brentford assets rather than invest, benching dilemmas and lots more!

Tomorrow on on Planet FPL: James presents the GW24 Deadline Stream, in partnership with FPL Team, live at 10am GMT

Today on Patreon: The Differential Show (BT+) and The Team News Stream, which will now be at 1030pm GMT tonight and available to all paying Patrons (BT)

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-120868390

Want to become a member of our FPL community and support the Podcast? 

Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl

