    <item>
      <title>Justin Time | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 32 | GW22 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Clayton and James discuss all the GW22 football from the weekend which was a bad one for their clubs sides and it was equally as bad in FPL too, with scores low and someone even managing to bench Justin Kluivert's monster 22 point return!

There's chat on an outstanding victory for Bournemouth at Newcastle, Arsenal's failure to see through a two-goal advantage against Aston Villa after Liverpool had left it late at Brentford, Manchester City showed what they are still capable of by hitting six at Ipswich and does James have a defence for Ange Postecoglu after a bewildering choice to play a back three at Everton? 

There's discussion on Everton and Liverpool assets for the upcoming double, James needs a Dominic Solanke replacement, should the likes of Raul Jimenez and Joao Pedro be moved on, Chris Wood went off again, what impact does William Saliba's injury have on Arsenal, Ruben Amorim's 'worst ever' Manchester United comment and lots more...

Tomorrow on on Planet FPL: People's Poll Podcast, vote for your choice of topic here before 530pm GMT Monday https://x.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1881303952186351940

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A (IT+) and Nico's Corner (AT)

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-120377210

Want to become a member of our FPL community and support the Podcast? 

