    <item>
      <title>Ipswich v Brighton | CotC with Paul Gaught-Allen &amp; Sam Murray | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Ipswich fan Paul Gaught-Allen and Brighton fan Sam Murray to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Thursday night's GW21 meeting at Portman Road.

Does anyone know if Joao Pedro is fit? And if so, he is could he be partnered again by returning Danny Welbeck.

With doubts over the Brighton pair does an in-form Liam Delap offer a sensible solution for FPL managers?

Do defenders such as Leif Davis and Jan Paul Van Hecke who may be owned from these clubs need binning?

Plus, discussion on Ipswich's chances for survival and continued frustrations about Brighton's inconsistencies.

Follow Paul on Twitter/x: https://x.com/fpl_tractor

Follow Sam on Twitter/x:https://x.com/FPLSeagull

Still to come today on the Planet FPL YouTube Channel, James presents The GW21 Deadline Stream, live and in partnership with FPL Team at 5pm GMT

Tomorrow on on Planet FPL: The Clayton &amp; James Show

Today on Patreon: The Differential Show GW21 Preview and The GW21 Team News Stream

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/119895820

