    <item>
      <title>He's Had Amad One | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 29 | GW20 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James review the weekend of Gameweek 20 which saw a massive Bryan Mbeumo 19 point haul at Southampton and many of the top sides drop points.

So, you're saying Tottenham and West Ham aren't top sides? Yes, but there was some positivity for Suj &amp; James to take from their sides performances despite defeats.

All the games covered including the concession of points from all of Chelsea, Arsenal and Liverpool and eyes turn to next Tuesday's Gameweek 21 with discussion including players to target from the likes of Crystal Palace and Newcastle, upcoming captaincy, concerns about owning multiple Arsenal defenders and Trent Alexander Arnold's nightmare performance will have caused concern for owners, and those looking to invest, with a Liverpool double Gameweek likely coming soon.

Tomorrow on on Planet FPL: The Fan View with new Leicester City Correspondent Sam Martin

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-january-119406536

