    <item>
      <title>From Across The Hall | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 25 | GW16 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>A tired James joins Suj to discuss the weekend football in Gameweek 16 which ended with Tottenham scoring five in the first half at St Mary's and Cole Palmer blanking in Chelsea's victory against Brentford. But Palmer wasn't the only big name FPL player to underwhelm this weekend where having the right differentials will have made the difference for many.

There's coverage of all 9 games as Arsenal and Liverpool both dropped points at home and City blew a lead late to lose the Manchester Derby.

And there are new FPL assets emerging to consider including the weekend's highest scorer Ismaila Sarr and a returning Diogo Jota, James has made an early transfer to bin the suspended Ryan Ait-Nouri, and there's a new FPL Chip to play with soon too!

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Fan View with Bradley Parker and Matt Samuel on Wolves and Southampton's decisions to sack their managers

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Away Days

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-dec-118066332

