    <item>
      <title>Chelsea v Brentford | CotC with Gary Mantle &amp; Tom Medd | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>James is joined by Chelsea fan Gary Mantle and Brentford fan Tom Medd to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Sunday's Gameweek 16 meeting at Stamford Bridge.

Are Chelsea now serious title contenders following Sunday's victory at White Hart Lane or are there too many concerns around aspects of their defence?

Can Brentford turn any of their incredible home form into success on the road or is the disparity in home v away results explained away by the quality of opponents faced?

Plus, FPL discussion includes whether man of the moment Cole Palmer should be captained this weekend, the appeal of enabler Enzo Fernandez, if Robert Sanchez and Levi Colwill are safe from further rotation and whether it's time to finally say goodbye for FPL managers who have held Brentford's players such as Mark Flekken, Bryan Mbeumo and Yoane Wissa.

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Brighton v Crystal Palace with Sam Murray and Ruaidhri McLoughlin-Dowd

Today on Patreon: My House Is Bigger Than Your House Quiz

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/117605615

Want to become a member of our FPL community and support the Podcast? 

