    <item>
      <title>Breaking Wind | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 24 | GW15 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James review the weekend of Gameweek 15 that saw us a game down following the postponement of The Merseyside Derby and the Podcast includes details of when the game may be rearranged to.

Unfortunately for those still on the Erling Haaland path, Mo Salah owners appear to have won again, with many moving the captaincy from Salah to Cole Palmer who returned with an 18 pointer in Chelsea's 4-3 victory at White Hart Lane which increased the pressure on Ange Postecoglu. Is James ready to call time on the Aussie's reign!?

Plus, analysis of all the games, info on those walking the suspension tightrope, defenders are on agenda but there aren't many that convince, should Bryan Mbeumo and Yoane Wissa really be sold after returning well against Newcastle, Gameweek 16 should look good on paper and there are well wishes for Michail Antonio. 

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: James presents his Ask James live stream at 12pm GMT with an audio posted shortly after conclusion

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Nico's Corner

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/117605615

