    <item>
      <title>It's Goin Down, I'm Yellin | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 23 | GW14 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Clayton joins James for a review of GW14 in a week where Arsenal won from corners and Tottenham lost from one, but that's not the only reason Tottenham lost, and James is in a mood this morning following the dismal showing at Bournemouth.

He did at least have some reason to cheer via FPL means as Alexander Isak was held and returned well in Newcastle's thrilling draw against Liverpool, but Mo Salah dominated again with another monster haul. The Egyptian King is now up to a barely believable 151 FPL Points for the season.

Clayton's gameweek meanwhile was somewhat saved by an Arsenal player and The Gunners ran out winners against a Manchester United team, who impressed with their structure, if not their threat.

All the games from Wednesday to Thursday covered, including Chelsea's demolition of Southampton, Aston Villa and Manchester City getting back to winning ways; whilst there's debate on FPL transfers as James seeks a new defender, there's a solution offered for Bryan Mbeumo owners, if those who have prersisted with Erling Haaland have to call it quits and is there enough reason to take Salah on with the captaincy this week?

...Tottenham might have offered one... but not for the right reasons.

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: James presents the GW15 Deadline Stream, in partnership with FPL Team, exclusively on the Planet FPL YouTube Channel at 10am GMT

Today on Patreon: The Differential Show and The Team News Stream

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/117134006

Want to become a member of our FPL community and support the Podcast? 

Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl

