    <item>
      <title>Bournemouth v Tottenham | CotC with Neil Grover &amp; Ricky Saunders | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Bournemouth fan Neil Grover and Tottenham fan Ricky Saunders to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Thursday's GW14 meeting on the South Coast.

Andoni Iraola's Cherries are impressing and fresh from an excellent victory at Wolves host a Tottenham side who continue to show inconsistencies and have a growing injury list.

Antonie Semenyo returns from suspension and will interest FPL managers but does Saturday's penalty hat-trick hero Justin Kluivert offer an even cheaper route for Fantasy managers into The Cherries attack?

There was another goal for Brennan Johnson at the weekend and his underlying data suggests there could be more to come, so why is he being overlooked by the majority of Fantasy managers and is he now the best asset from the league's top scorers.

Plus, there's discussion on Evanilson and Dominic Solanke, who, sickness permitting, is set to face his old club, there's concern over the goalkeeping situations at both clubs and there's advice for those who want to buy or invest in the likes of Milos Kerkez and Pedro Porro

Thursday on Clash of the Correspondents: Fulham v Arsenal with Lewis James and Adam Pritchard

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Clayton &amp; James Show Ep. 17

Today on Patreon: The Differential Show and The Team News Stream

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/117134006

