    <item>
      <title>Manchester United v Everton | CotC with Gary Robinson &amp; Sean Norton | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>James is joined by Manchester United fan Gary Robinson and Everton fan Sean Norton to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Sunday's Gameweek 13 meeting at Old Trafford.

There's Fantasy discussion on United assets with Bruno Fernandes proving popular in recent weeks but has the time passed to invest and should those who have invested in Fernandes and other United assets be looking to sell following this weekend?

And Everton assets are for the bin with a horrendous fixture schedule on the horizon, or is there a case to hold on to some of their assets?

Plus, there's discussion on the manager situations, with reaction to Ruben Amorim's opener at Ipswich and who might become a part of the new man's best eleven as we approach 2025; and with a takeover by the Friedkin Group imminent at Everton, Sean Dyche's days in charge could be running out....

Next week on Clash of the Correspondents: Manchester United v Everton with Gary Robinson and Sean Norton

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Clayton &amp; James Show Ep. 16

Today on Patreon: UCL Fantasy MD5 Preview &amp; Nico's Corner

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-nov-25-116672625

