    <item>
      <title>Over And Under Performance | The People's Poll ep. 154 | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>Clayton joins James to have a look at some of the data from the opening 11 weeks in the Premier League and have a discussion about which teams are and aren't overperforming.

There's discussion on performance versus expected goals, expected goals conceded and expected points, using data from fbref and Understat.

There's also coverage on using context for statistics such as factoring in the quality of opponents, why some data isn't sustainable for some teams, the cut off between the bottom 7 and the rest, explainers for some underperformers, considering what's next and more.

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clayton and James Show

Today on Patreon: Quiz and Slack Stories

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/115773430

