    <item>
      <title>The Dominator | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 19 | GW10 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Clayton joins James to discuss the weekend fixtures from Gameweek 10 with Mo Salah captainers doing well, but many other popular assets misfired, which included the majority of James' team, infact all of James' team misfired, but it was somewhat saved from being the Gameweek from hell by Dominic Solanke!

And the Tottenham forward was also a surprise selection as part of Clayton's Wildcard which has performed well.

On the Pod, discussion on all the games includes why James was confident Bournemouth could upset Manchester City, Newcastle's tactical structure that nullified Arsenal, Chelsea intrigued but failed to see off Ruud Van Nistelrooy's 'good lads' of Manchester United and fears for Gary O'Neil at Wolves only intensified after a 2-2 draw with Crystal Palace.

And FOMO might have hit James for the first time this season... 

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: People's Poll Podcast, vote for your choice of topic here before 5pm GMT https://x.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1853407352982003737

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Nico's Corner 

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/115329476

