    <item>
      <title>Ipswich v Leicester | CotC with Paul Gaugh-Allen &amp; Aaron Lagor | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Ipswich fan Paul Gaught-Allen and Leicester fan Aaron Lagor to discuss one of Saturday's bif 6 pointers at the bottom of the table at Portman Road.

Ipswich remains winless and now have injuries and suspensions causing major alarm, particularly in the backline. While though Leicester can be pleased with their return so far of 1 point per game Friday's defeat to Nottingham Forest has dampened the mood.

There's discussion on the relegation scrap, tactics and selection options for Saturday, prospects for FPL assets such as Leif Davis and Jamie Vardy and whether the real FPL opportunity with these two clubs should come, not from investing in them, but in attacking players about to face them!

Follow Paul on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fpl_tractor

Follow Aaton on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AaronLagor

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Fan View with Gary Robinson on Manchester United's decision to sack Erik Ten Hag

