    <item>
      <title>Walking On Hot Cole | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 14 | GW6 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss the 9 games from the Premier League weekend and there was some wild swings for Fantasy managers, and particularly many on Wildcard which included Suj, and for many it ended in disappointment. There's discussion on thinking longer-term for Wildcard and that decisions aren't made based on just one Gameweek.

But for James, who Wildcarded back in week 3, it was a stormer and Cole Palmer's monster 25 point haul helped him rise inside the nose bleed territory of the top 50k. But what should Palmer owners who have gone without do now? Does structure and upcoming fixtures necessitate continuing to go without?

All the games covered as usual which include the North London clubs posting some silly underlying numbers, Liverpool's win that took them top, Villa being held by Ipswich and it's getting tiring talking about the shortcomings of Manchester United!

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: People's Poll Podcast - A statistical look at the first 6 Gameweeks of the season

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Slack Stories

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-sep-30-113050626

