    <item>
      <title>Four Letter Words | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 12 | GW4 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>On the Gameweek 5 Review Suj and James discuss all the games from the weekend and it was a particularly painful one for James following defeat in the North London Derby. Discussion on Arsenal's victory and how they overcame the absence of Declan Rice and Martin Odegaard.

But it wasn't all bad news for James in FPL as Ollie Watkins matched another Erling Haaland haul and it was another successful weekend for Suj who included Gabriel in his starting eleven.

Plus, for many Wildcarders there may be regret as Liverpool assets flopped in a surprise defeat to Nottingham Forest and a theme of this week's review is a hunt for decent forward options.

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: People's Poll Podcast with Clayton and James

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Nico's Corner

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-sep-112149674

