    <item>
      <title>Women's Football Season Preview | with Lauren Harris | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>James is joined by Planet FPL Women's Football Correspondent Lauren Harris for a chat about Women's Football ahead of the kick of the new Women's Super League season next week.

There's discussion on Emma Hayes following her success with the US national team and what her departure from Chelsea may mean for The Blues with Arsenal and Manchester City set to challenge again for the title. Can any of those three go all the way in the Champions League and can anyone else from the WSL challenge them in the domestic competitions?

Plus, there's discussion about the growth of The Championship and the battle to get into the WSL which includes not only the likes of Newcastle United but also Michelle Kang's London City Lionesses.

And the England Lionesses are discussed ahead of next summer's Euros and there's discussion on attending Women's Football including James' experience at last season's Women's FA Cup Final.

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Clayton &amp; James Show ep.5

Today on Patreon: UCL Fantasy Watchlist &amp; Nico's Corner

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-sep-9th-111706497

