    <item>
      <title>Tweak Of The Thumb | Planet FPL S. 8 Ep. 10 | GW3 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss the fallout from all the Gameweek 3 games as Erling Haaland made it back-to-back hat-tricks for another seventeen points and Mo Salah match that total as Liverpool cruised to victory at Old Trafford. It mean owning both with the captaincy on either returned 51 points, and despite James' Wildcarding he's still sitting there with neither. So how bad did it turn out!?

All the games and key talking points discussed with a heavy focus on the FPL assets on mind both for the shorter term and thinking further ahead; plus James is pleased despite Tottenham's defeat at Newcastle, and for Manchester United there's a feeling that things won't change until there is change. 

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Manchester City v Brentford with Jonny Pringle and Tom Medd

Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Nico's Corner

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/111255735

