    <item>
      <title>Man Utd v Liverpool | CotC with Gary Robinson &amp; Dan Lord | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Manchester United fan Gary Robinson and Liverpool fan Dan Lord to talk FPL assets and their clubs ahead of what many perceive as English's football biggest fixture.

There's discussion on the two clubs start to the season, with concern for what the reaction may be at United if defeat at Brighton is followed by another loss and how much we can read from Liverpool's opening two wins.

There's advice for those on Manchester United assets in FPL including whether Bruno Fernandes and Alejandro Garnacho should cut their losses and the majority of Liverpool assets can be considered but there is agreement on two standouts, the danger of 'no' Salah and whether there would a preference for double Liverpool attack or defence.

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream, scheduled for 2pm BST with an audio posted shortly after conclusion

Today on Patreon: Money in Football &amp; Talking Tactics

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-august-110842417

