    <item>
      <title>Wolves v Chelsea | CotC with Bradley Parker &amp; Gary Mantle | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>On the opening of Clash of the Correspondents for 2024/25 James is joined by Wolves fan Bradley Parker and Chelsea fan Gary Mantle to discuss current matters and FPL assets at their clubs ahead of Sunday's meeting at Molineux.

As the closure of the transfer window approaches both clubs are in very different positions. Despite recouping close to £100m after the sales of Max Kilman and Pedro Neto (to Chelsea) the club reportedly only have £20m to invest; whilst at Chelsea the spending continues and more can be expected before the transfer window shuts, but the club is trying to sell several players with up to 15 reportedly told they don't have a future at the club and that includes Raheem Sterling.

There's discussion on what Chelsea can expect from Neto and what may now be their strongest line-up and where Wolves may look to spend what is available to improve their current squad.

Plus, FPL discussions feature a strong interest in Chelsea assets with a good fixture list on the horizon. The Christopher Nkunku and Cole Palmer debate is re-evaluated and if they can be trusted defensively to invest. But The Blues recent record at Wolves is not good, and might the best FPL investment defensively from the two clubs be in the home side?

Follow Bradley on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/parker_bradley

Follow Gary on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/Phantomantle

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream at 12pm BST with an audio to follow shortly after.

Today on Patreon: Money in Football on Girondins De Bordeaux, and Talking Tactics on the opening to Newcastle v Southampton

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-aug-110373127

