    <item>
      <title>Leicester with Aaron Lagor | Correspondent Week ep.19 | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>Aaron Lagor joins James to discuss all things Leicester City and their FPL assets ahead of their Monday night Gameweek opener against James' Tottenham. But despite being the Championship Champions they currently don't feel as strong as they did when achieving promotion.

Why? Manager Enzo Maresca and key player Kiernan Dewsbury-Hall have departed for Chelsea. Former Nottingham Forest manager Steve Cooper is Maresca's replacement and there's a detailed debate on what may be different under the new manager.

For FPL club legend Jamie Vardy may still lead the line, while wide men Abdul Fatawu and Stephy Mavididi are also 5.5. Should any of the trio appeal for investment?

And there are enablers to consider with Wout Faes (4.0) and Harry Winks (4.5) both well owned.

But you may listen to this Podcast and want to have a second look at Tottenham assets and The Foxes also look set for a points deduction.

Follow Aaron on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/AaronLagor

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.20 Liverpool with Dan Lord

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/109354364

