    <item>
      <title>Fulham with Lewis James | Correspondent Week ep.13 | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>It's a Planet FPL debut for new Fulham Correspondent Lewis James on the opening Podcast of Day 4 on Correspondent Week and with a very attractive set of fixtures to begin with there's plenty of interest in their FPL assets. But how will they cope with the departure of the brilliant Joao Palhinha?

There's detail on new additions including Emile Smith-Rowe and a returning Ryan Sessegnon, and more additions can be expected to a squad that is likely to be led up front by Rodrigo Muniz who will prove popular for those looking for a reliable cheaper forward.

Bernd Leno has been a proven consistent goalkeeper in Fantasy, but he may be overlooked with Fulham's backline all priced at 4.5. There's a debate about the prospects for Timothy Castagne and Antonee Robinson.

Plus, could Smith-Rowe's arrival mean a departure for Andreas Pereira, and if so, who would take over set-piece duties. The answer may surprise. And there's also detail of why we may see a back three from Fulham as the season progresses.

Follow Lewis on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/LewisFFCJames

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.14 Brighton with Sam Murray

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/109354364

