    <item>
      <title>Everton with Sean Norton | Correspondent Week ep.5 | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>Planet FPL Correspondent Mini-League Winner Sean Norton joins James to kick off Day 2 of Correspondent Week by discussing all things Everton including interest in their FPL assets, particularly the defensive one's.

The Toffees go into this season having had two attempted club Takeovers collapse and it's to be their final campaign at Goodison Park. What would constitute making their final season at their current home a success? Does it need to be more than just survival?

There will be interest in Everton defensive assets but Jordan Pickford, Jarrod Branthwaite and James Tarkowski are now 5.0. Should managers look at a 4.5 alternative for coverage?

Plus, there's discussion on Everton's new signings and whether Dominic Calvert-Lewin can be relied upon to lead the line on a consistent basis.

Follow Sean on on Twitter: https://twitter.com/spirit_blues

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.6 Manchester United with Gary Robinson

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/109354364

