    <item>
      <title>Brentford with Tom Medd | Correspondent Week ep.3 | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>Brentford fan Tom Medd joins James to discuss The Bees ahead of the new season including whether we should expect more from a club who suffered badly with injuries. But the injuries look like they may persist with new signing Igor Thiago out injured until the winter and with major problems persisting at full-back.  

Will Ivan Toney stay or go? That's the major headline into The Bees season but if he stays will he even start in Gameweek 1? 

Bryan Mbeumo is currently an attractive differential in FPL, but FPL managers may be put off by Brentford's three challenging away trips inside the first five gameweeks; and Tom wants to make the case for a different attacker from the club.

And Mark Flekken is currently the most owned 4.5 keeper but could his position in the team be under threat and do any of the 4.5 defenders at the club offer a better or safer alternative?

Follow Tom on on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPLDummyTom

Next on Correspondent Week: ep.4 West Ham United with Chris Stone

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/109354364

