    <item>
      <title>England After Southgate | The People's Poll ep. 146 | Planet FPL 2024/25</title>
      <description>A week on from Gareth Southgate's decision to stand down as England manager, Suj and James reflect on Southgate's tenure, discuss what might be next with the next manager and ask what England fans want England to be.

There's praise for what Southgate has achieved both on and (especially) off the pitch, including how he united the team; but there's also acknowledgement that the time was probably right for him to step aside.

But will what's next be better? Who should get the job? And there's details on The FA's job remit of what they are looking for from applicants.

And what do fans and the media want from England? Is it more attractive football and fluid tactics or ultimately is the result at major tournaments what still matters most?

Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Pilot episode of The Clayton and James Show

Today on Patreon: Away Days, Queens Park Rangers 20/7/24

For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/108586060

