    <item>
      <title>See You In October | Planet SkyFF S.6 Ep.1 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>With the Premier League TV selections confirmed for August and September, Suj and James discuss thoughts for Sky Fantasy planning and assess which clubs Fantasy managers will 'need' coverage of and which clubs will be 'wanted'.
(Yes you can listen to this at any point in the next month if you want to revisit it!)
There's a surprising lack of single gamedays in the opening 6 matchweeks, James details why this is the case and what it means on early transfer count usage; there's discussion on potential early gains and why some players will appeal over others as we approach the season kick off on August 16th.
For those who would like to watch back last season's 'Intro To Sky Fantasy' Podcast here is the link 
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LDB5xkV9zgE&amp;t=47s
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet FPL on Euro 2024 with a review of the France v Spain semi final and a preview of England v Netherlands
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Down The Pub (extended cut)
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-schedule-107727762
