    <item>
      <title>Mods And Cons | Planet FPL On Euro 2024</title>
      <description>Clayton joins James to discuss the latest for Euro Fantasy and last night's conclusion to Group B as Spain's second string team beat Albania and Croatia are nearly out after Italy scored a 98th minute equaliser which means a possible end to Luka Modric's International career.
And in the second half of the Podcast there's discussion on England and the intel suggests it will be one change with Connor Gallagher replacing Trent Alexander-Arnold. There's reaction to the news, what Clayton and James would do, a look ahead, knowing that irrespective of the result tonight, England are through to the last 16, but how important is it that they win the Group?
If you want to join our Euro Fantasy mini league the code is - 1LoPXq  
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: A review of tonight's games in Groups C and D
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and Twitter Stories
