    <item>
      <title>Saved By The Bell | Planet FPL On Euro 2024</title>
      <description>Suj and James review the opening three days at The Euros as the favourites all won bar a Denmark side that were held by Slovenia prior to England's victory over Serbia in Gelsenkirchen... but not everyone is happy.
There's a detailed analysis and explanation for why the game got tougher for England in the second half and why it's okay to not be happy but also be content with what happened.
There's coverage of Euro Fantasy dilemmas including whether to stick or twist for owners who have had a captaincy return but perhaps not the haul they wanted, whether it should be Lukaku or Mbappe for those twisting today and options not considered are emerging ahead of Matchday 2.
If you want to join our Euro Fantasy mini league the code is - 1LoPXq  
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clayton and James review Monday's 3 games at The Euros
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-june-106348382
