    <item>
      <title>Burnley v Nottingham Forest | CotC with Jack Toner &amp; Mark Sutherns | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Burnley fan Jack Toner and Nottingham Forest fan Mark Sutherns to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Sunday's final day meeting at Turf Moor.
For Burnley, relegation was confirmed following defeat at Tottenham and it's felt like an inevitability for some time but the club has kept faith with manager Vincent Kompany and their inexperienced squad should be in a good position to challenge to come straight back... or is there reason for concern?
Forest are safe, bar an unlikely 12 goal swing on final day. But it has been a bad season and their safety is only due to the inability of the three teams below. What's gone wrong? And what are the club likely to do next? Could key players depart? And will Nuno Espirito Santo be kept on?
Plus, goals are expected when the two clubs meet on Sunday, so should FPL managers look at enablers such as Jacob Braun Larsen or Callum Hudson-Odoi as a source for points in Gameweek 38?
Follow Jack on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/TurfyTopper
Follow Mark on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/FFScout_Mark
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet SkyFF s5 ep45
Today on Patreon: Premier League Final Day Quiz and The Unanswered Qs
