    <item>
      <title>West Ham v Luton | CotC with Chris Stone &amp; Dan Ashby | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <description>James is joined by West Ham fan Chris Stone and Luton fan Dan Ashby on Clash of the Correspondents to discuss the latest at their clubs and preview Saturday's meeting in East London.
It's been a dramatic week for The Hammers, a 5-0 beating at Chelsea was followed by the news that David Moyes will leave the club at the end of this season with former Wolves manager Julen Lopetegui widely being reported to be his replacement. There's discussion on Moyes' tenure and the potential new boss.
The Hatters meanwhile are three points from safety with two to play and the decision that Nottingham Forest's points deduction will stand means there is still hope, but two wins will probably be needed. Can they get the win they need against a West Ham team that has only won 3 league games in 2024?
Plus, likely summer departures, looking ahead to next season and are FPL managers right to overlook these two teams this weekend?
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: James presents The GW37 Deadline Stream Live in partnership with FPL Team exclusively on the Planet FPL YouTube Channel at 10am BST
Today on Patreon: The Differential Show and The Team News Stream
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-may-7th-103787643
