    <item>
      <title>Flake Diss Track | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 51 | GW36 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss another dramatic week in FPL where the top 10k average hit 100 and James exceeded that to enter into the top 100k but for Suj, the less said the better!
All the games reviewed as usual which included Suj and James teams getting slapped respectively and conceding a combined 9 at Stamford Bridge and Anfield. And Manchester United didn't want to be left out as they crumbled to a 4-0 loss at Crystal Palace last night.
The title race continues to look like it will go down to the wire as Arsaenal and Manchester City recorded comfortable victories which featured Erling Haaland scoring four and Nottingham Forest claimed a crucial victory at Sheffield United.
Amongst the analysis of the games is a heavy focus on FPL assets for Double Gameweek 37 and the final day and many FPL managers will have a defensive crisis on their hands ahead of the Double but the closer it gets the more it feels like single gameweek players shouldn't necessarily be overlooked and there are solutions offered for Bruno Fernandes owned if Manchester United's talisman doesn't make it for trhe double.
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet SkyFF s5 ep44
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A, UCL Fantasy Bitesize and Away Days
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-may-7th-103787643
