    <item>
      <title>Chelsea v Tottenham | CotC with Gary Mantle &amp; Ricky Saunders | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents it's a focus on the only two teams who double in Gameweek 35 as James is joined by Chelsea fan Gary Mantle and Tottenham fan Ricky Saunders to discuss the latest at their clubs and talk about the best FPL assets from each club with many Wildcarders this week look to load up with 3 from each ahead of their two double gameweeks in 35 and 37.
But neither are in good form! A Chelsea without Cole Palmer were destroyed 5-0 at Arsenal on Tuesday night and it wasn't much better for Tottenham who lost 4-0 at Newcastle 12 days ago. There's discussion on Mauricio Pochettino's future and whether defeat to rivals Tottenham next week could see the process begin for a change in the dugout. While some frustrations are beginning to creep in to the mindset of Tottenham fans and there is trepidation ahead of Sunday's North London Derby.
Plus, best FPL assets discussed. Cole Palmer will be a certainty for most and so to will Heung-Min Son despite form concerns. But who else should FPL managers be investing in? Or, should they just be avoiding altogether!?
Follow Gary on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/Phantomantle
Follow Ricky on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/Rickysaunders77
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: s7 ep49, the midweek review of GW34
Today on Patreon: Ask James live stream and Nico's Corner
