    <item>
      <title>Thinker Failure Occurred | Planet SkyFF S.5 Ep.41 with Phil Loveland-Stuart &amp; Shaun Thorpe</title>
      <description>James is joined by Planet FPL Patrons Phil and Shaun to discuss to discuss all the latest hot topics for Sky Fantasy Football and it was largely a failed 'moving day' on Sunday as the majority of Arsenal and Liverpool assets blanked. Next Wednesday offers another opportunity to make a heavy number of changes. But should we be looking to move before then?
There's discussion on Crystal Palace and Everton assets with Sunday in mind, best Arsenal captaincy choices for Saturday against Wolves and then Chelsea (or should be Cole Palmer!?) on Tuesday, if it's got to be Mo Salah on Sunday and thoughts on moves for next Wednesday, ehich could become particularly awkward if Manchester City's fixture at Brighton moves forward 24 hours from the Thursday.
Plus, data learnings, differentials under consideration, what the penultimate matchweek 37 fixture announcement changes in plans and lots more.
Follow Phil on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/failure_fpl
Follow Shaun on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/FF_Thinker
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream at 12pm BST with an audio to follow shortly after conclusion
Today on Patreon: The Q'N'A with host David Hunter and Chip Talk on a DGW34 Free Hit
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-april-102373754
