    <item>
      <title>Fulham v Newcastle | CotC with Dara Curran &amp; Simon Bibby | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents it's a meeting of the black and whites as James is joined by Fulham fan Dara Curran and Newcastle fan Simon Bibby to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Saturday's meeting at Craven Cottage.
Both clubs have had troubles on the road this season as seen again this week with Fulham, who followed some brilliant victories by conceding six across two games at Sheffield United and Nottingham Forest. So they'll be pleased to be at home this weekend against a Newcastle side who have also struggled on the road.
Does that mean a home win is likely with the Fulham frontline likely to be spearheaded again by the in-form Rodrigo Muniz against a Newcastle side that is again suffering through injuries defensively?
There's discussion on the FPL relevant assets of interest including Muniz and other Fulham players that managers may own, plus the all important Newcastle assets who have a great run of fixtures that leads towards their double in the penultimate gameweek of 37. Alexander Isak, Anthony Gordon, Harvey Barnes and yes, the best choice of the defensive assets is covered too!
Follow Dara on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/TheTinkerMen
Follow Si on Twitter/x: https://twitter.com/fplBibs
Friday on Planet FPL: Planet FPL s7 ep45 GW31 Review Podcast
Today on Patreon: Premier League Goalkeepers Quiz
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-march-101416876
