    <item>
      <title>Mo Muniz Found | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 44 | GW30 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>It's a late Sunday night Podcast for Suj and James to discuss all the fallout from Gameweek 30 ahead of the quick turnaround for Tuesday's Gameweek 31 deadline.
There's discussion on the drab Man City-Arsenal encounter that means it's now advantage Liverpool in the title race following their victory against Brighton. There's rage at West Ham's defeat at Newcastle having led 3-1, Tottenham came from behind again to beat a spirited Luton, how a bright start for Wolves fizzled out at Villa and somehow Brentford nearly lost despite dominating Manchester United.
There's FPL relevant discussion on every club with many managers planning their routes towards either Gameweek 34 or 37 but many may be hampered again by a sea of flags and that includes to popular Chelsea and Newcastle assets that may make life difficult for current Wildcarders.
And it was such a good week for Suj that James looks set to copy his moves for GW31 in a bid to captain Mo Salah.
Tuesday on Planet FPL: *NOT* The GW31 Deadline Stream, Live stream at 12pm GMT. Audio to follow shortly after
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-march-101416876
Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
Follow Clayton on Twitter: https://twitter.com/claytsAFC
Subscribe to our YouTube channel: https://www.youtube.com/@PlanetFPL
Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
#FPL #ChipStrategy #GW30Review
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
