    <item>
      <title>Man New Players Wanted | Planet SkyFF S.5 Ep.38 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss all the latest for Sky Fantasy Football and that includes the key information on the latest TV selections for the end of April and with Tottenham now not given a fixture in the midweek set of fixtures there are several teams that have 3 for 0s that might even be 4 for 0 over the North London club.
Arsenal and Liverpool will appeal to Sky managers over that period but James is also keen to make the case for Manchester United and Newcastle assets who will currently be lowly owned.
Plus, exit points not just for Tottenham assets but the likes of Ollie Watkins and Dominic Solanke covered, planned captaincy and transfer thoughts for the week ahead are also discussed and listener questions debated.
Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ham and Nico's Corner
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Nottingham Forest v Crystal Palace with Mark Sutherns and Ruaidhri Mcloughlin-Dowd
