    <item>
      <title>Fans Anger At Fixture Scheduling | The People's Poll ep. 142 | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <description>Clayton joins James for a discussion on what goes into arranging fixtures in the Premier League and the influence of TV companies that often leaves match going fans unhappy.
Who's involved in moving a fixture to a particular date and time?
Why do fans get so angry about delayed movements of fixtures?
And there's discussion on the battle between the rival TV companies and how their eagerness to stitch each other up leads to fans losing out, including those watching on TV and there's strong views on why fixtures with permutations on further possible movements must stop.
Today on Patreon: An Intro To Fantasy Challenge and Chip Talk: GW30 Wildcard
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet SkyFF s5 ep38
