    <item>
      <title>Blank Canvas | Planet SkyFF S.5 Ep.36 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss all the latest Talking points for Sky Fantasy with only 9 teams participating over the upcoming week and for many it will be a week to take stock rather than invest again after a period where many have taken advantage of gains.
But that's not the case for everyone...
Should those without investment in Bournemouth-Luton tonight buy Dominic Solanke or consider a Luton alternative?
Jarrod Bowen vs Ollie Watkins is the debate for Sunday's captaincy and for those who haven't gone for investment in Tottenham should that be amended as a priority ahead of Saturday's trip to Fulham?
Plus, learnings from the weekend, why selling Brighton assets may need to be reconsidered, buying a new goalkeeper, investment in Arsenal after the Internationals, listener questions and more.
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, West Ham v Aston Villa with Chris Stone and Lee Jackson
Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ars and Nico's Corner
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/100146453
