    <item>
      <title>Making An Arse Of It | Planet SkyFF S.5 Ep.35 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>Suj and James discuss the latest for Sky Fantasy Football and the fallout from the investment in Arsenal on Monday night, which wasn't as big as we may have expected and for a certain someone there was no investment in The Gunners at all!
Investment plans for what's to come now focus on Aston Villa, Tottenham and West Ham on Sunday and Chelsea or Newcastle or Monday. But the solutions of who to buy seems quite straightforward, it's just a case of how heavy Sky Fantasy managers invest with only 4 fixtures to focus on during the following weekend. But a certain someone (yep him again) might not be able to buy anyone on Sunday!
Plus, captaincy for the weekend, coverage of next Wednesday's Bournemouth-Luton encounter, thoughts for further ahead, listener questions, learnings from the weekend, approaching the point of set and forget and more...
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream at 12pm GMT with an audio to follow shortly after
Today on Patreon: Money in Football on Wolves' finances and Nico's Corner
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-march-99704372
