    <item>
      <title>Bourne Ready | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 40 | GW27 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James review all the weekend Gameweek 27 football with an eye on the Bournemouth-Luton upcoming Double and what's beyond in GWs 29 and 30.
How big should FPL managers commit to the two doublers? Is Dominic Solanke the definite go-to captain for the Gameweek? And with James on the hunt for a defender there's a theme of looking at defensive assets throughout this Podcast.
As usual all the games reviewed, including Alphonse Areola hauling at Everton, Heung-Min Son rewarding buyers with a goal late on against Crystal Palace, Villa leaving it late at Luton and the Sunday wins for Bournemouth and a Phil Foden inspired Manchester City.
A Foden who James might even bench in GW28!
There's lots to discuss and that includes why Brighton might be about to move the landscape for FPL managers again.
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The People's Poll Podcast, vote for your topic of choice before 5pm GMT here: https://x.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1764610962617745450?s=20
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A &amp; The Unanswered Qs
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-march-99704372
