    <item>
      <title>Gunning For Cherries | Planet SkyFF S.5 Ep.34 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>On the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast Suj and James discuss all the latest talking points ahead of a period where there are a lot of gains to be made and there could be a lot of transfers confirmed!
We're all buying Dominic Solanke on Sunday - or are we? There are now concerns about a knee injury for the Bournemouth talisman, so what should we do if he's not passed fit?
There will also be moves made for Arsenal assets on Monday but how big should Sky managers go on the high-flying Gunners?
Plus, learnings from the weekend, upcoming captaincy and there's discussion on the partial announcement of April TV fixtures and why it can be covered with just 4 teams!
Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ham, with all the latest on Tottenham and West Ham including a review of that Jarrod Bowen hat-trick
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet FPL s5 ep39, with the latest on Chip Strategy following the fallout from the FA Cup games
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/99224753
