    <item>
      <title>Man Utd v Fulham | CotC with Gary Robinson &amp; Dara Curran | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents is James is joined by Manchester United fan Gary Robinson and Fulham fan Dara Curran to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of Saturday's Blank Gameweek 26 meeting between the clubs at Old Trafford.
It's 4 wins on the spin for United in the Premier League including 3 hard fought away victories and they are back in contention for Champions League qualification. But are they actually convincing anyone that they've truly turned the corner?
Are Fulham truly safe from overlooking their shoulder? They should be, but their away form is terrible and have tough home fixtures to come and will have to cope for the next 2 games without the instrumental Joao Palhinha who is suspended.
Plus, there's discussion on the best FPL assets from above. Rasmus Hojlund is in great goalscoring form while enabling Fulham forward Rodrigo Muniz is also on a streak. But can FPL managers find a way to fit either forward in?
There's also discussion on the keepers who are among the highest scoring in FPL this season, best defensive assets from above and if any of the differential midfield options can be considered including an ever improving Alejandro Garnacho.
And somehow, this Podcast survives two power cuts to reach a conclusion.
Today on Patreon: The Quiz on 1 Club Men and Nico's Corner
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet SkyFF s5 ep33
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/98751963
