    <item>
      <title>Ayew Sure Elsa!? | Planet SkyFF S. 5 Ep. 32 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>On the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast Suj and James discuss all the big talking points including the upcoming Manchester City and Liverpool fixtures next week.
And those aren't the only upcoming single gamedays coming up, with Wolves v Sheffield United and West Ham v Brentford next week those games need to be kept in mind, but first it's Crystal Palace's trip to Everton. Skip? Invest? Chain on to the next single gamedays? There's a detailed look at the best (and worst) Everton and Palace assets for Monday.
Plus, should Cole Palmer be sold because of upcoming gains? Does similar apply to Tottenham assets? Upcoming captaincy, learnings from the weekend, how Arsenal hurt non owners, listener questions and more.
Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ars and the 4 Big Mac challenge
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: People's Poll Podcast on planning for GW29
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-12th-98316960
