      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>Suj and James discuss all the latest for Sky Fantasy Football including the impact of Monday's announcement of the March TV fixtures and there weren't any huge shocks in the announcement that mean longer-term planning can begin with the caveat of understanding that FA Cup results and a potential Bournemouth v Luton announcement may mean plans needs to change.</p><p>There's discussion on learnings from the last week including concern about Tottenham defensive players, captaincy for the weekend ahead, why some big template players should be sold in the near future, Everton's sudden appeal and if Mo Salah, if available should be forced straight back in.</p><p>And For James it was a particularly good week that has seen him enter the top 200 for the first time this season.</p><p>Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ham and Chip Talk</p><p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Luton Town v Sheffield United with Dan Ashby and Ben Thompson</p><p>For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/97881178</p><p>Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? </p><p>Join us on Patreon: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl">https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl</a></p><p>Follow James on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod">https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod</a></p><p>Follow Suj on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/sujanshah">https://twitter.com/sujanshah</a></p><p>Follow Clayton on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/claytsAFC">https://twitter.com/claytsAFC</a></p><p>Subscribe to our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@PlanetFPL">https://www.youtube.com/@PlanetFPL</a></p><p>Like us on Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl">https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl</a></p><p>Follow us on Instagram: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl">https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl</a></p><p>#SkyFF #SkyFantasy #SkyFantasyFootball</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>]]>
