    <item>
      <title>Chipping In Again | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 32 | Chip Strategy Special | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Suj and James present an updated Chip Strategy Podcast following last weeks domestic Cup matches and yesterday's all important FA Cup 5th round draw. What's changed? What's still not clear and what do we need to know?
Is there clarity now on what will be the most popular chip strategy?
There's discussion on the immediate problem of negotiating Double Gameweek 25 and Blank Gameweek 26, updated projections for the later Blank and Double Gameweeks, the best weeks to play the chips that remain and different strategies as to how FPL managers may want to do it.
There's conclusions on locking in Plan A vs Plan B, James' favoured strategy, what could happen with the yet unscheduled games and lots more.
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The Fan View with Dan Lord on Jurgen Klopp's announcement that he will leave Liverpool at the end of the season
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and The Unanswered Qs
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/schedule-jan-feb-97403480
