    <item>
      <title>Chipping In | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 29 | Chip Strategy Special | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>It's the first big Chip strategy Podcast of the season as Suj and James layout a roadmap of what to expect during the second half of the season with blank and double gameweeks and the various options available for Chip strategies.
There's discussion on a now 'probable' Double Gameweek 25 for Liverpool, what could happen to the unfulfilled fixtures featuring Manchester City and Bournemouth and an understanding of the blank and double gameweeks to come during the season.
There's analysis of what weeks will be popular for Chip usage of the Bench Boost, Free Hit, Triple Captaincy and the second Wildcard and why working out when to Free Hit may be defining. Is there a current optimal strategy?
Plus, why too much Liverpool, Chelsea and Tottenham could cause a major GW26 problem that may also be repeated in GW29; why the end of season doubles may be crap for Fantasy managers and the fallout from the weekend including Arsenal losing again, the fitness status of Jarrod Bowen and Erling Haaland and Tottenham's likely purchase of Timo Werner.
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: SkyFF s5 ep27 with the final discussion ahead of Overhaul for Sky Fantasy
Today on Patreon: Get The F Out Quiz and The Unanswered Qs
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/96059135
