    <item>
      <title>Sick And Dom | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 26 | GW18 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>On the Gameweek 18 Review Podcast Suj and James discuss more fun with flags as several FPL managers see their teams decimated by injuries and suspensions and for many those problems are defensively, and with cash spare in many a FPL managers bank balance Trent Alexander-Arnold is now a priority for many. But it won't be for everyone...
Meanwhile Dominic Solanke netted a hat-trick at Forest, managed for the first time by Nuno Espirito Santo, Liverpool and Arsenal shared the points in the top of the table and the bottom 3, written off by many, all had great results including Sheffield United, who denied Aston Villa a place at the top of the table on Friday night.
While Suj and James go into Christmas celebrating home victories for their clubs; a limp Manchester United were comfortably dispatched by West Ham, for Tottenham it was a far more difficult assignment against a revitalised Everton.
Tuesday on Planet FPL: James presents the GW19 Deadline Stream in partnership with FPL Team, Live at 10am GMT on the Planet FPL YouTube channel
Tomorrow on Patreon: The Differential Show GW19 Preview
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-dec-24th-95233013
