    <item>
      <title>Sparring Partners | Planet SkyFF S. 5 Ep. 23 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>Fixture guru and all round Sky Fantasy ledge Ian Parrin joins James on the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast and there's plenty to cover as we approach the festive period.
On the agenda, Erling Haaland, buy/sell/keep, solutions, actions taken. The lack of goalkeeper options with a number injured and who is under consideration. Sunday's Brighton entry point, has it got to be Pascal Gross? Can Lewis Dunk be risked? Or is there another who can be considered?
Plus, learnings from the weekend, upcoming captaincy, the final midweek of January TV picks, tips for post Overhaul considering the absence of Mo Salah and Heung-Min Son, when City v Brentford might drop and listener questions covered.
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: People's Poll Podcast. It's an FPL theme, pick your favourite from these on Twitter/x before 530pm GMT - https://x.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1734901008667435138?s=20
Today on Patreon: Quiz - Hosted by Dan Lock on Boxing Day's in the Premier League
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-dec-11th-94462307
