    <item>
      <title>The Wild Vice Card | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 24 | GW16 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>Another dramatic weekend of football for FPL managers, which included an injured Erling Haaland missing out for Manchester City and bug returns for Mo Salah and Heung-Min Son. While for James, multiple problems on top of the Haaland news prompted James to pull the trigger on Wildcard on Saturday night 2 weeks earlier than planned.
While for Suj, despite having the vice captaincy on Mo Salah, he still scored less than a Salah-less James. But at least he didn't say Fulham wouldn't score 5 goals against West Ham last Friday... ...oh yes he did!
All the games reviewed as Villa extended their incredible winning run, Tottenham finally turned a good performance into a good resullt against a walking wounded Newcastle, Bournemouth won comfortably at Old Trafford and Chelsea were humbled at an Everton who are 3 from 3 and no goals conceded.
The Podcast also has a theme of options under consideration for James' Wildcard and Planet FPL won a trophy this weekend!
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Chelsea v Sheffield United with Gray Mantle and Ben Thompson
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A and The Unanswered Qs
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-dec-11th-94462307
