    <item>
      <title>Dunked In Gross Stuff | Planet SkyFF S. 5 Ep. 21 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <description>On the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast Suj and James to discuss all the latest for Sky Fantasy which is about to feature the first Premier League midweek fixtures of the season.
There's discussion on Lewis Dunk's yellow and red card combo at Nottingham Forest and why that makes owning him or planning to buy him a nightmare, so what are the solutions for the two Brighton single gamedays if Dunk isn't the play?
Plus, upcoming captaincy for the weekend and next midweek covered, transfer ideas if Jarrod Bowen's injury is longer than expected, the complications around Chelsea players, secondary Arsenal coverage, if the additional Man City-Brentford, learnings from the weekend, the Wolves gamble that took place on Monday night against Fulham, listener questions and more...
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, West Ham v Crystal Palace with Chris Stone and Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd
Today on Patreon: Tot&amp;Ham
