    <item>
      <title>Tasty Nachos | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 21 | GW13 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>It always seemed likely to be a tough weekend for Fantasy managers with many faced with conflicting issues and that has proved to be the case for many, including Suj and James, who reflect on their underwhelming weekends during the Gamewwek 13 Review.
All the games discussed including another mad Tottenham game that ended in defeat to Villa side that's up to 4th, West Ham won it late, as did Arsenal who went top following the City-Liverpool draw, while Chelsea lost heavily at Newcastle, it was a great weekend for Luton and Alejandro Garnacho scored one of 'the' great Premier League goals at Goodison Park.
FPL thinking discussed, including why Jarrod Bowen's fitness will determine what many will do, there's a number of misfield enablers suddenly putting their hand up for consideration, prospects for going double defence - including Arsenal, GW14 captaincy, Matt(y) Cash concerns, Reece James, why those who are planning to Wildcard in GW19 may have just been given a gift by the injury Gods...
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Nottingham Forest v Everton with Mark Sutherns and Sean Norton
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-nov-27th-93603935
