    <item>
      <title>Tsimi On Down | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 19 | GW12 Review | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <description>After the 'anyone got points?' carnage of GW11, Suj and James review an extraordinary GW12 weekend which concluded with an all time classic between Chelsea and Manchester City and opened with Tottenham losing late on at Wolves. Newcastle were humbled at Bournemouth, while Erling Haaland and Mo Salah both returned 16 pointer, but many FPL managers benched Kostantinos Tsimikas' 15 point haul in Liverpool's victory against Brentford.
All the games covered, there's discussion on defensive FPL assets, why GW13 looks ugly for many, the importance of recognising when teams are missing key central midfield players, upcoming fixture swings, FPL assets of interest and lots more...
Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Newcastle United v Chelsea with Simon Bibby and Gary Mantle
Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A
For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-nov-13th-92791278
