      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>After the 'anyone got points?' carnage of GW11, Suj and James review an extraordinary GW12 weekend which concluded with an all time classic between Chelsea and Manchester City and opened with Tottenham losing late on at Wolves. Newcastle were humbled at Bournemouth, while Erling Haaland and Mo Salah both returned 16 pointer, but many FPL managers benched Kostantinos Tsimikas' 15 point haul in Liverpool's victory against Brentford.</p><p>All the games covered, there's discussion on defensive FPL assets, why GW13 looks ugly for many, the importance of recognising when teams are missing key central midfield players, upcoming fixture swings, FPL assets of interest and lots more...</p><p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Newcastle United v Chelsea with Simon Bibby and Gary Mantle</p><p>Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A</p><p>For the full Planet FPL schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-nov-13th-92791278</p><p>Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? </p><p>Join us on Patreon: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl">https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl</a></p><p>Follow James on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod">https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod</a></p><p>Follow Suj on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/sujanshah">https://twitter.com/sujanshah</a></p><p>Follow Clayton on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/claytsAFC">https://twitter.com/claytsAFC</a></p><p>Subscribe to our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@PlanetFPL">https://www.youtube.com/@PlanetFPL</a></p><p>Like us on Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl">https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl</a></p><p>Follow us on Instagram: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl">https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl</a></p><p>#FPL #FantasyPremierLeague #GW12Review</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>]]>
