    <item>
      <title>Newcastle v Crystal Palace | CotC with Simon Bibby &amp; Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/newcastle-v-crystal-palace-cotc-with-simon-bibby-ruaidhri-mclaughlin-dowd-planet-fpl-202324</link>
      <description>On the first of three Clash of the Correspondents during this International break James is joined by Newcastle fan Simon Bibby and Crystal Palace fan Ruaidhri McLaughlin-Dowd to discuss the latest at their clubs ahead of the GW9 meeting between the two at James' Park.
 Ten points from the last 4 in the league from the Toon Army which included five consecutive clean sheets across three competitions, there's been a 4-1 beating of PSG in the Champions League and an 8-0 away win at Sheffield United and it's meant FPL assets, particularly defensively are of interest.
 But it's Palace who current have the highest scoring goalkeeper in FPL (Sam Johnstone) and the highest scoring defender (Joachim Andersen!). And despite a growing and concerning injury list The Eagles find themselves only 1 point behind Newcastle in the table.
 Is Kieran Trippier worth the 2 million or so more than the other Newcastle defenders in FPL? And if not who is the best from the cheaper assets?
 Does Marc Guehi at 0.4 cheaper than teammate Andersen worth consideration now The Dane is approaching the 5.0 mark?
 Plus, can Callum Wilson or Alexander Isak be invested in despite injury and rotation concerns? How much should Fantasy managers be considering Anthony Gordon and can Palace find the way to goal with Michael Olise still unavailable and talisman Ebe Eze now sidelined? 
 ...and does this have the potential to be last on Match of the Day.... again?
 Follow Si on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fplBibs
 Follow Ruaidhri on Twitter: https://twitter.com/R_P_MD
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream at 12pm BST with an audio version to follow
 Today on Patreon: Money in Football on Match Fixing in English Football
 For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: 
 https://www.patreon.com/posts/89442472
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Follow Clayton on Twitter: https://twitter.com/claytsAFC
 Subscribe to our YouTube channel: https://www.youtube.com/@PlanetFPL
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 #NUFC #CPFC #FPL
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
