    <item>
      <title>An Ollie Controversy | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 13 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/an-ollie-controversy-planet-fpl-s-7-ep-13-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj and James review all the football so far in Gameweek 7 which featured huge controversy, particularly at White Hart Lane with Luis Diaz having a goal disallowed which was clearly onside. 
 James sets a 10 minute timer to explain anger at what was arguably the worst piece of refereeing in Premier League history, despite the fact victory took Tottenham up to second.
 The rant is followed by discussion on all the games including Villa's mauling of Brighton as Ollie Watkins scored a monster 23 points to take him top of the FPL points scoring chart ahead of Erling Haaland who blanked as Manchester City were beaten at Wolves.
 Plus, all the FPL assets of interest discussed as West Ham and Jarrod Bowen come into our thinking, there's injury updates, tactical thoughts and whether Heung-Min Son is deserving of the Gameweek 8 armband...  
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: When To Wildcard, a look at now versus December
 Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A
 For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: 
 https://www.patreon.com/posts/90159270
