    <item>
      <title>Luton v Burnley | CotC with Dan Ashby &amp; Jack Toner | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/luton-v-burnley-cotc-with-dan-ashby-jack-toner-planet-fpl-202324</link>
      <description>It's a Double Gameweek special on Clash of the Correspondents as James is joined by Luton Town fan Dan Ashby and Burnley fan Jack Toner to discuss the latest at their clubs and the all important FPL assets ahead of the two clubs meeting next Tuesday at Kenilworth Road which is part of a Double Gameweek for both.
 Is Carlton Morris the standout captaincy option from the two clubs and if so is it worth taking Erling Haaland on with the armband?
 Best enabling defensive options from both clubs covered and there are as many as 7 assets at 4.0 or under who are worth deliberating for Fantasy managers, including the now 3.9 Charlie Taylor; but will he stay in the team?
 And are there any midfield options that can be considered from the two clubs? 
 Plus, the battle to beat the drop and the current media narrative around both clubs, with many already writing Luton off, but some predicting an upturn in results possible for Burnley...
 Follow Dan on Twitter: https://twitter.com/danlukeashby
 Follow Jack on Twitter: https://twitter.com/TurfyTopper
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Women's Super League Preview with Lauren Harris
 Today on Patreon: Money In Football on Football Piracy
