    <item>
      <title>Rotation Roulette | The People's Poll ep. 132 | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/rotation-roulette-the-peoples-poll-ep-132-planet-fpl-202324</link>
      <description>How much should Fantasy managers be concerned about upcoming rotation? There's a look at 'rest' days' in the upcoming calendar for those playing in the Champions League and why Sunday games could cause particular concerns for the Europa qualifiers.
 Does the threat or rotation help or hinder those who wish to take Haaland on during City's difficult run?
 Are concerns over Newcastle rotation overplayed or justified? 
 Will Arsenal and Manchester United likely to go strong with their core players regularly?
 How seriously will Villa, Brighton, Liverpool and West Ham treat their Thursday nights games?
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet SkyFF s5 ep11 with all the latest for Sky Fantasy Football
 Today on Patreon: UCL Fantasy Final Drfats
 For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: 
 https://www.patreon.com/posts/89442472
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
