      <title>Time For A Comeback | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 11 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/time-for-a-comeback-planet-fpl-s-7-ep-11-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James discuss the 9 games at the weekend in what was a difficult Gameweek 5 for many Fantasy managers as the majority of favoured players underwhelmed, including Tottenham players despite the dramatic late victory against Sheffield United.
 What's wrong with Manchester United and Chelsea? Have FPL managers got to bin the likes of Marcus Rashford, Ben Chilwell and Nicolas Jackson?
 Plus, there were narrow victories for Arsenal and Newcastle to discuss, rotation concerns will grow with European football starting, Villa and Liverpool players have increasing appeal and Julian Alvarez causes disagreements and it was a weekend of comebacks...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The People's Poll, vote available here on Twitter: https://x.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1703719773350035466?
