    <item>
      <title>Spending Cash With Gusto | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 8 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/spending-cash-with-gusto-planet-fpl-s-7-ep-8-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj and James assess all the games played in a dramatic Gameweek 3 that included late wins for Manchester City and Liverpool on Sunday, Arsenal dropping points at home to Fulham and West Ham briefing going top after a stunning victory at Brighton.
 FPL mid priced midfielders appear to be top of the agenda for many managers with several showcasing their talent as again at the weekend including James Maddison and Raheem Sterling who hauled against Luton on Friday night.
 Sterling was not the only player who hauled from Chelsea as 4.0 (now 4.1) Malo Gusto went big in the same fixture and fellow right-back Matty Cash scored twice for Aston Villa at Turf Moor.
 Should underperforming big named stars be binned? Who should managers show greater patience with? And should we consider having 8 starting attackers? 
 Plus, lots more including coverage of every game.
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet SkyFF s5 ep8 with all the latest for Sky Fantasy Football
 Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A
 For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week, including our offering on Patreon view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/88365471
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
