      <title>Chelsea v Luton | CotC with Gary Mantle &amp; Dan Ashby | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/chelsea-v-luton-cotc-with-gary-mantle-dan-ashby-planet-fpl-202324</link>
      <description>James is joined by Chelsea fan Gary Mantle and Luton Town fan Dan Ashby to discuss the latest at their clubs, the all important FPL assets at them and preview Friday's night's GW3 opener at Stamford Bridge.
 It's only 1 point from the first two for Mauricio Pochettino's Blues. Is there cause for concern ahead of the incredible upcoming fixture run or is there reason for optimism despite the slow start?
 The Hatters will have waited 13 days for this following the opening weekend defeat at Brighton. Are The Hatters likely to try and frustrate on Friday or can they view the game as a free hit with their own brilliant fixture run set to start in GW4?
 Plus, all the important FPL assets covered, especially from The Blues where several assets appeal and there's a couple of Luton players that should remain in Fantasy managers thinking too...
 Follow Gary on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Phantomantle
 Follow Dan on Twitter: https://twitter.com/danlukeashby
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Planet SkyFF s5 ep7, with all the latest discussion for Sky Fantasy
 Today on Patreon: The Transfer Window Show 
 For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week view this post: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
