    <item>
      <title>Boosted Vitamins | Planet FPL S. 7 Ep. 6 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/boosted-vitamins-planet-fpl-s-7-ep-6-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>On the first Gameweek Review of the season Suj &amp; James discuss the 9 games played at the weekend and all the relevant fallout for FPL managers.
 But first there's discussion on the drama before deadline surrounding the Manchester City team news and the rumoured absence of Arsenal's Gabriel.
 There's discussion on the FPL assets that interest most now that we've seen them play, what John Stones and Gabriel owners should do, the season's first bandwagon might not be a bandwagon at all. Plus, there's tactical insight to the games watched, including discussion on Arsenal's 3-1-6, Villa's high line that got shredded at Newcastle, Chelsea's unexpected setup.
 And what about that Bench Boost? Was it successful for James...?
 And do Salah owners dare captain the Egyptian King over Erling Haaland in GW2?
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream at 12pm BST with an audio version to follow
 Today on Patreon: The Patreon Q'N'A
 For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week view this post: www.patreon.com/posts/content-aug-14th-87649352
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
