      <title>Everton with Sean Norton | Correspondent Week ep. 18 | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/everton-with-sean-norton-correspondent-week-ep-18-planet-fpl-202324</link>
      <description>On James’ fixture planner for the first 8 gameweeks the team that appears top of the difficulty ratings, is Everton. Can they take advantage and get off to a good start despite concerns that they’ll be involved near the bottom of that table again?
  And if so are there FPL assets to consider? The answer is almost definitely yes.
  Jordan Pickford, James Tarkowski and Ashley Young may all appeal defensively but the gem might be 4.0 Jorrod Branthwaite. Could he start the season?
  And at the top end Arnaut Danjuma and Dominic Calvert-Lewin – subject to fitness – could also be considered and as we find out on the Podcast there may even be a gem who is yet to be given a price.  
  Follow Sean on Twitter:  https://twitter.com/spirit_blues
  Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 19 – Arsenal with Adam Pritchard, Saturday 10am BST 
  Today on Patreon: The Correspondent Week Debrief with Suj: on Sheffield United, Newcastle, Bournemouth and Chelsea
  For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/86901192
  Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
  Join us on Patreon:  https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
  Follow James on Twitter:  https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
  Follow Suj on Twitter:  https://twitter.com/sujanshah
  Follow Clayton on Twitter:  https://twitter.com/claytsAFC
  Subscribe to our YouTube channel:  https://www.youtube.com/@PlanetFPL
