    <item>
      <title>Chelsea with Gary Mantle | Correspondent Week ep. 16 | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/chelsea-with-gary-mantle-correspondent-week-ep-16-planet-fpl-202324</link>
      <description>Gary Mantle joins James for a particularly important Correspondent Week Podcast on Chelsea who are now managed by former Tottenham manager Mauricio Pochettino and have a number of important and interesting FPL assets that appeal, particularly ahead of a critical fixture swing in Gameweek 3.
  But Christopher Nkunku ‘might’ be injured, should he be fit he is still very much worth considering, but so to is the slightly cheaper Nicolas Jackson.
  Reece James vs Ben Chilwell, which is best for investment? Or should 4.5 Levi Colwill take Fantasy managers defensive investment? Or should, with concerns about depth in midfield, Chelsea’s defence be avoided all together?
  Plus, 4.5 midfielder Carney Chukwuemeka looks set to start in GW1, is he one of the 8 Chelsea players Gary thinks (subject to fitness) are locked to start vs Liverpool? 
  Follow Gary on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Phantomantle
  Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 17 – Burnley with Jack Toner, Friday 7pm BST 
  Today on Patreon: The Correspondent Week Debrief with Suj: on Sheffield United, Newcastle, Bournemouth and Chelsea
  For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/86901192
  Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
  Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
