    <item>
      <title>Sheffield United with Ben ‘Tommo’ Thompson | Correspondent Week ep. 13 | Planet FPL 2023/24</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/sheffield-united-with-ben-tommo-thompson-correspondent-week-ep-13-planet-fpl-202324</link>
      <description>The task looked tough already with spending likely to be restricted, critics writing them off and now star signing Ilman Ndiaye has left for Marseille. Ben ‘Tommo’ Thompson joins James to discuss The Blades chances of silencing the critics and to discuss a number of interesting enabler options for FPL.
  Right wing-back George Baldock is proving popular but will he start regularly enough to justify investment?
  And we find out it could be a bench full of Blades for FPL managers with 4.5 midfield and forward options who may emerge.
  Plus, likely starting eleven, find out who’s nicknamed ‘League One’, and there’s injuries… lots of them!
  Follow Tommo on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPL_Blade
  Next on Correspondent Week: ep. 14 – Newcastle United with Simon Bibby, Thursday 7pm BST 
  Today on Patreon: The Correspondent Week Debrief with Suj: on Manchester United, West Ham, Fulham and Tottenham
  For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/86901192
  Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
  Join us on Patreon:  https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
