      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>On the final Premier League Clash of the Correspondents of the season James is joined by Leeds fan Andy Martin and Tottenham fan Ricky Saunders to discuss the latest at their clubs and what is a must win game for both on Sunday at Elland Road.</p> <p>But a win might not be enough...</p> <p>Can Leeds overhaul Everton and Leicester on final day and stay up?</p> <p>Can Tottenham better Aston Villa's result and qualify for Europe? (Do they even want to?)</p> <p>There's discussion on the (farcical) managerial and ownership situation at both clubs and best FPL assets for final day in a game that will almost certainly provide goals...</p> <p>Follow Andy on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/fpl_tactician">https://twitter.com/fpl_tactician</a></p> <p>Follow Ricky on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/Rickysaunders77">https://twitter.com/Rickysaunders77</a></p> <p>Tomorrow on the Planet FPL: James presents <em>NOT</em> The GW38 Deadline Stream Live at 4pm BST with an audio version to follow shortly after conclusion.</p> <p>Today on Patreon: A Quiz on Premier League final days hosted by @FPLGas76</p> <p>For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week view this post: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/posts/83362826">https://www.patreon.com/posts/83362826</a></p> <p>___________________________________________</p> <p>Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? </p> <p>Join us on Patreon: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl">https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Follow James on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod">https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod</a></p> <p>Follow Suj on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/sujanshah">https://twitter.com/sujanshah</a></p> <p>Like us on Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl">https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Follow us on Instagram: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl">https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>#Leeds #Tottenham #FPL</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>]]>
      </content:encoded>
