    <item>
      <title>Leicester v Liverpool | CotC with @AaronLagor &amp; @FPL_LocoLord | Planet FPL 2022/23</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/leicester-v-liverpool-cotc-with-aaronlagor-fpl_locolord-planet-fpl-202223</link>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Leicester fan Aaron Lagor and Liverpool fan Dan Lord to discuss the latest at their clubs, the Monday night meeting at The King Power and the FPL assets of interest.
 Can Leicester save themselves from the drop? Do they now have to win on Monday? There's also reflection on Brendan Rodgers reign as manager and thoughts on the interim spell under Dean Smith.
 Liverpool are on a run of 6 consecutive wins and have found form just in time to keep themselves in contention for a top 4 finish, can they yet overhaul one of the United's above them?
 Plus, are we overlooking captaining Mo Salah this week? Surely Trent Alexander-Arnold can't be benched... and with Leicester better offensively than defensively and desperate for points could the likes of James Maddison and Harvey Barnes be differentials to consider?
 And expect goals...
 Follow Aaron on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AaronLagor
 Follow Dan on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPL_LocoLord
  Still to come today: James presents *Not* The GW36 Deadline Stream Live at 530pm BST with an audio version also posted later this evening
 Today on Patreon: The Differential Show gw36 Preview
 For the full Planet FPL Schedule this week view this post: https://www.patreon.com/posts/82733720
