    <item>
      <title>Brentford v Aston Villa | CotC with @FPLDummyTom &amp; @Lee_Jackson_92 | Planet FPL 2022/23</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/brentford-v-aston-villa-cotc-with-fpldummytom-lee_jackson_92-planet-fpl-202223</link>
      <description>On the first Podcast of a Clash of the Correspondents Triple this week James is joined by Brentford fan Tom Medd and Astron Villa fan Lee Jackson to discuss all the latest at heir clubs and the important FPL assets ahead of Blank Gameweek 32.
 Toney? Watkins? Both or neither? FPL managers Free Hitting this week may well be having this exact dilemma, but it's not just with the forwards where this dilemma exists and the Podcast also features discussion on Raya and Martinez as options this week.
 There's also thoughts on when or if assets should be sold for those who own, as both do have difficult fixtures remaining this season.
 But Brentford have proved they can beat the league's best and Villa are on a run so good that they have every right to believe they can qualify for Europe...
 Follow Tom on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPLDummyTom
 Follow Lee on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Lee_Jackson_92
 Today on Patreon: It's Money In Football on the Premier League's next television deal and a UCL Fantasy Bitesize Podcast
