    <item>
      <title>Tottenham v Bournemouth | CotC with @Rickysaunders77 &amp; @AFCBNG | Planet FPL 2022/23</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/tottenham-v-bournemouth-cotc-with-rickysaunders77-afcbng-planet-fpl-202223</link>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Tottenham fan Ricky Saunders and Bournemouth fan Neil Grover to discuss all the latest at their clubs ahead of Saturday's Gameweek 31 meeting at White Hart Lane.
 Can Tottenham still make a push for a top 4 finish? There's discussion on the interim appointment of Cristian Stellini and who may get the manager's job permanently in the summer.
 While quietly Bournemouth have put a run together and look capable of pulling themselves clear from the bottom 3, can they continue their run?
 Plus, all the important talking points for FPL, icluding the prospect of captaining Harry Kane this weekend and whether Gameweek 32 Free Hitters should have him in their side and why the likes of Philip Billing and Dominic Solanke should remain a strong consideration for FPL managers in coming weeks.
 And Leicester get mentioned a lot...
 Follow Ricky on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Rickysaunders77
 Follow Neil on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AFCBNG
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Ask James live stream @ 5pm BST with an audio version published shortly after
 Today on Patreon it's a Quiz on the relegation battle
 Full the full Planet FPL Schedule this week including the offering on Patreon see this post... https://www.patreon.com/posts/content-apr-10th-81280644
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? 
