    <item>
      <title>Drugdealer | Planet SkyFF S. 4 Ep. 32 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/drugdealer-planet-skyff-s-4-ep-32-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>On the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast it's a moment to pause during the International Break and discuss what's to come for the remainder of the season and there's every reason to still think gains can be made.
 Erling Haaland's ownership in the top 1000 has taken a major dive. Will managers buy him straight back for the Liverpool fixture with no obvious fixture gain back to the City forward?
 There's coverage of confirmed fixture movements in April following the European and FA Cup results, why differentials such as James Maddison, Ollie Watkins and Wilfried Zaha, yes Wilfried Zaha could appeal for investment in April.
 Plus, thoughts on selling Arsenal assets, how big the investment in Liverpool may be throughout the month and lots more...
 On Planet FPL tomorrow: The Fan View on Tottenham with @Rickysaunders77
 On Patreon today it's Tot&amp;Ham with all the latest on a dramatic week for Tottenham
 For the full schedule of content for this week view this post 🗓 Content Schedule: March 20th-24th | Planet #FPL with Suj &amp; James on Patreon
