    <item>
      <title>Mismatch Of The Day | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 38 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/mismatch-of-the-day-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-38-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>On the review of the Gameweek 27 a largely underwhelming start for the popular Brentford and Brighton doublers as many FPL managers benched or sold Arsenal assets who stormed to victory at Fulham and Liverpool slipped to defeat at Bournemouth.
 There's insight into all the games including Tottenham's victory against Forest, Manchester City's tactical victory against Palace, how Leeds forced change on Brighton and the impact of Casemiro on the want for Manchester United assets in DGW29.
 Plus, what Free Hitters are likely to do in GW28, why Wildcarding this week should still be considered for those who haven't used it and why transfers in this week are liklely to focus on Aston Villa, Chelsea and Newcastle players... and James has gone early and bought one of them already...  
 On Planet FPL tomorrow: Clash of the Correspondents, Chelsea V Everton with @Phantomantle &amp; @spirit_blues
 On Patreon today it's the Patreon Q'N'A
 For the full schedule of content for this week view this post 🗓 Content: Mar 13th-17th | Planet #FPL with Suj &amp; James on Patreon
