    <item>
      <title>That Chip Strategy Podcast 3 | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 36 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/that-chip-strategy-podcast-3-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-36-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James discuss all the permutations for strategy following a set of shocking result in The FA Cup as Leicester, Southampton and Tottenham all lost to lower league opposition. Is Wildcarding NOW the obvious solution for FPL managers who have landed badly for Double 27, Blank 28 and Double 29?
 James discusses permutations for later in the season for those who want to take advantage of Doubles in 34 and 37 and several different options are discussed with some certainly favoured over others. Can those who do choose to Wildcard now keep up with those who Wildcard later in the season?
 There's coverage of all the teams with a summary of who to target immediately, who to come back to, fixture swings and so much more including a reminder of the consciousness of GW35...
 Plus there's a conclusion of GW25 following wins for Arsenal and Liverpool last night.
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: NOT The GW26 Deadline Stream Live at 530pm GMT on the Planet FPL YouTube channel with a Podcast of the stream released later in the evening.
 On Patreon today it's tTot&amp;Ham: And reaction to those FA Cup defeats
 For the full schedule of content for this week view this post 🗓 Content: Feb 27th-Mar 3rd | Planet #FPL with Suj &amp; James on Patreon
 ___________________________________________
