    <item>
      <title>Liver Little | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 34 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/liver-little-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-34-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>On the Gameweek 24 review, all eyes for FPL managers turn towards the rarely sighted Blank Double Gameweek of 25 as 4 teams Blank and 4 teams Double but who from the Blankers should be binned and which of the Doublers should be invested in?
 All the games reviewed, which included another swing in the title race, Tottenham won the Planet FPL derby, there were big 1-0 wins for Bournemouth, Everton and Southampton at the foot of the table, Fulham defied the stats to win by the same score at Fulham, Chelsea's defeat has led to many to call for Potter's dismissal, Liverpool put themselves back in contention for 4th with victory at ten man Newcastle and Marcus Rashford rewarded those who captained him ahead of Erling Haaland.
 Plus, why thinking beyond GW25 can influence transfer decisions for this coming gameweek, why there's likely to be big Liverpool gambles, expected minutes for enablers this week and why for James selling one of his premium forwards need to be considered...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: People's Poll Podcast, vote for your favourite from the options on Twitter before 5pm GMT. 
 On Patreon today it's the Patreon Q'N'A
 For the full schedule of content for this week view this post 🗓 Content Schedule: Feb 20th-24th | Planet #FPL with Suj &amp; James on Patreon
