    <item>
      <title>Rash Decisions | Planet SkyFF S. 4 Ep. 27 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/rash-decisions-planet-skyff-s-4-ep-27-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>On the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast Suj is up to his old tricks of missing deadlines! Did it work in his favour or does it feel like the 50k prize now out of reach?
 There's discussion on why after a week with heavy investment on Arsenal and Man City this is likely to be a quieter week for transfers accept for those who have sold Harry Kane.
 Should Haaland be captained on Saturday or should there be concerns about rotation? And who's best for Sunday with Kane and Marcus Rashford likely to divide opinion?
 Plus, should Wolves be invested in now ahead of their single gameday next Friday at Fulham? Awareness of the right Chelsea point and how the additional Brighton-Palace and Southampton-Brentford alters planning...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Money In Football - The Premier League's decision to charge Manchester City with numerous breaches of financial rules
 On Patreon today it's Planet FPL s6 ep33b as we discuss the fallout from Liverpool's victory against Everton and Man City's crucial victory against Arsenal last night
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 #SkyFF #SkyFantasy #SkyFantasyFootball
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
