    <item>
      <title>Nulty Planning | Planet SkyFF S. 4 Ep. 26 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/nulty-planning-planet-skyff-s-4-ep-26-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>Paul McAnulty from the 3 For 1 Sky Fantasy Football Podcast joins James for this week's Sky Fantasy Football Podcast and he's currently got two teams in the top 100 of the overall standings!
 There's discussion on Paul's strategy of following the template, how it works for him and at what point he'd consider moving from it if he's in contention to come first.
 Plus, the template captaincy picks look straightforward for the week ahead, learnings from the weekend, what the new additional March 1st mean to planning, consciousness of the Fulham-Wolves single gameday, awareness of what else could change in March and there are big gains to be had coming up for Arsenal, Liverpool and Manchester City; but who's worth investing in? And should Manchester United and Newcastle assets be sold on mass?
 Follow Paul on Twitter: https://twitter.com/paulmcanulty1
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents - Arsenal vs Manchester City with @ThreeFiveWho &amp; @FPLPringle
 On Patreon today it's a special Ask James (About Tottenham). Patrons can find the link to the stream which starts at 4pm GMT via this post 🐓Ask James (About Tottenham) Live Stream | Planet #FPL with Suj &amp; James on Patreon
 ___________________________________________
