        <![CDATA[<p>Paul McAnulty from the 3 For 1 Sky Fantasy Football Podcast joins James for this week's Sky Fantasy Football Podcast and he's currently got two teams in the top 100 of the overall standings!</p> <p>There's discussion on Paul's strategy of following the template, how it works for him and at what point he'd consider moving from it if he's in contention to come first.</p> <p>Plus, the template captaincy picks look straightforward for the week ahead, learnings from the weekend, what the new additional March 1st mean to planning, consciousness of the Fulham-Wolves single gameday, awareness of what else could change in March and there are big gains to be had coming up for Arsenal, Liverpool and Manchester City; but who's worth investing in? And should Manchester United and Newcastle assets be sold on mass?</p> <p>Follow Paul on Twitter: https://twitter.com/paulmcanulty1</p> <p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents - Arsenal vs Manchester City with @ThreeFiveWho &amp; @FPLPringle</p> <p>On Patreon today it's a special Ask James (About Tottenham). Patrons can find the link to the stream which starts at 4pm GMT via this post <a href="https://www.patreon.com/posts/ask-james-about-78380354">🐓Ask James (About Tottenham) Live Stream | Planet #FPL with Suj &amp; James on Patreon</a></p> <p>___________________________________________</p> <p>Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Join us on Patreon: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl">https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Follow James on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod">https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod</a></p> <p>Follow Suj on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/sujanshah">https://twitter.com/sujanshah</a></p> <p>Like us on Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl">https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Follow us on Instagram: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl">https://www.instagram.com/plane