    <item>
      <title>Marc Of Greatness | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 32 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/marc-of-greatness-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-32-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James review all the Gameweek 22 games and all the relevant talking points which included Marcus Rashford rewarding the 500,000+ FPL managers who Triple Captained him.
 Imagine a weekend where none of Arsenal, Chelsea, Liverpool or Manchester City scored, yep that happened and there's analysis of why all four had struggles. They weren't the only ones and there's pressure on the managers on Bournemouth, Leeds and Southampton after they also all failed to score as well.
 Plus, there's focus on the next double with the top 2 set to face off next week, awareness of a potential Liverpool double gameweek and for James it was an emotional day as Harry Kane became Tottenham's all time record goalscorer... 
 *Please note this Podcast was recorded prior to the Premier League's charges against Manchester City for breaches of financial rules*
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents: Fulham vs Nottingham Forest with @TheTinkerMen &amp; @FFScout_Mark
 On Patreon today it's a Quiz on the January Transfer Window
 For the full schedule of content for this week view this post 🗓 Content Schedule: Feb 6th-10th | Planet #FPL with Suj &amp; James on Patreon
 ___________________________________________
