    <item>
      <title>March Through February | Planet SkyFF S. 4 Ep. 25 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/march-through-february-planet-skyff-s-4-ep-25-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>On the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast there's discussion what we've learned about upcoming fixtures following the Cup results and the announcement of the March TV fixtures.
 Could there be additional fixtures added to the schedule? (Spoiler, yes)
 Should assets from the clubs who have a game postponed for the Carabao Cup Final be sold? And if so, then when?
 Plus, potential big gains to be had around the scheduled Cup games, captaincy for the weekend including the range of choices for Saturday, if Chelsea and Fulham assets should be sold following their Friday night single gameday, why Arsenal continue to standout, Man City thoughts following the Joao Cancelo sale, if Leeds should be invested in on Sunday and more...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: That Chip Strategy Podcast 2 with discussion on understanding blanks and doubles and Chip Strategy ideas.
 On Patreon today it's Tot&amp;Ham with discussion on the FA Cup victories, James travels to Preston and the closure of the transfer window.
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? On Planet FPL Patreon in January all Patrons will be boosted to the next tier level.
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
