      <content:encoded>
        <![CDATA[<p>An open discussion about the spending and revenues of the Premier League versus the other big five leagues and the trends are suggesting that England's top flight clubs are operating ona different level to clubs around Europe.</p> <p>There's a look at transfer spending, Television deals and matchday revenue and if the Premier League's growth can be stopped. Could something happen that means income declines? And should we care if it doesn't...?</p> <p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents - Manchester United vs Leeds United with @ismyCAPplaying &amp; @fpl_tactician</p> <p>On Patreon today it's the Patreon Q'N'A</p> <p>___________________________________________</p> <p>Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? On Planet FPL Patreon in January all Patrons will be boosted to the next tier level.</p> <p>Join us on Patreon: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl">https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Follow James on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod">https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod</a></p> <p>Follow Suj on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/sujanshah">https://twitter.com/sujanshah</a></p> <p>Like us on Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl">https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Follow us on Instagram: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl">https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>#PremierLeague #TransferWindow #FootballFinances</p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>]]>
      </content:encoded>
