    <item>
      <title>Please Don't Go Early | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 30 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/please-dont-go-early-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-30-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>On the Gameweek 21 review Podcast Suj &amp; James cover the 9 Premier League games played at the weekend and the fallout from them ahead of what will probably be Double Gameweek 22 but might not be.
 Erling Haaland punished those who didn't captain him with another home hat-trick but Arsenal responded to City's win with a dramatic victory against Manchester United and with their own double gameweek in 23 to come there's detail on favoured Arsenal and City assets.
 United and Leeds assets receive coverage ahead of their potential 22 double and Marcus Rashford Triple Captain is very much under consideration for James.
 Plus, an analysis of all the other games including Liverpool's uninspiring draw with Chelsea and there's a reminder why there are so many reasons why this week, more than any other in the whole season, is not the week to make early transfers...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: The People's Poll Podcast. Vote for your favourite topic from these 3 options before 5pm GMT  https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1617463243470954502?s=20&amp;t=djC9e4jfwzBLaljOEl4GzQ
 On Patreon today it's a the weekly Patreon Q'N'A
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? On Planet FPL Patreon in January all Patrons will be boosted to the next tier level.
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
