    <item>
      <title>The Future Of Domestic Cups | The People's Poll ep. 119 | Planet FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/the-future-of-domestic-cups-the-peoples-poll-ep-119-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>Last Friday there was a meeting between chairs of the Premier League, The FA and the EFL and one of the key talking points was how the domestic football calendar may have to change from the 2024/25 season.
 On this Podcast Suj &amp; James discuss why the revamp of the European competitions means that something will have to give in the domestic calendar.
 Will teams who have qualified for Europe have to field development teams in the Carabao Cup?
 Why can't those teams just withdraw from the competition?
 Will this be the end of FA Cup replays?
 And could The Community Shield be played abroad?
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL: Clash of the Correspondents, Everton v Southampton with @spirit_blues &amp; @CS_Wipeout
 On Patreon today it's the Patreon Q'N'A
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? On Planet FPL Patreon in January all Patrons will be boosted to the next tier level.
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 #FACup #CarabaoCup #UEFA
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
      <pubDate>Mon, 09 Jan 2023 12:07:19 -0000</pubDate>
