    <item>
      <title>Overhaul Surprises | Planet SkyFF S. 4 Ep. 19 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/overhaul-surprises-planet-skyff-s-4-ep-19-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>On the Sky Fantasy Football Podcast Suj &amp; James discuss all the important talking points ahead of Monday's Premier League resumption. 
 There's coverage of top 1000 ownership currently, captaincy for the week ahead including Kane v Salah for Monday and there's a look ahead to gamedays that could cause managers a headache including a Saturday that may cause issues despite there being 7 fixtures!
 That could be because Manchester City fixture gains are hard to ignore, but which City assets are best to select? Aston Villa and Leeds assets are covered ahead of their January single gameday, all of the Big 7 are covered as well as Fulham who have up to 4 single gamedays before the end of February and there's discussion on the thinking behind current drafts.
 Plus, there's a look at what postponed games could be added to the schedule in January.  
 On Planet FPL Patreon, in January all Patrons will be boosted to the next tier level. Support the show at www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 On Friday: FPL Drafts - A sense check of what Suj &amp; James are planning to go with in FPL
 And on Patreon today it's Tot&amp;Ham
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? On Planet FPL Patreon, December is FREE for existing Patrons! And in January all Patrons will be boosted to the next tier level.
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
