    <item>
      <title>Man Utd v Nott'm Forest | CotC with @ismyCAPplaying &amp; @FFScout_Mark | Planet FPL 2022/23</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/man-utd-v-nottm-forest-cotc-with-ismycapplaying-ffscout_mark-planet-fpl-202223</link>
      <description>On the final Clash of the Correspondents before the resumption of the Premier League James is joined by Manchester United fan Gary Robinson and Nottingham Forest fan Mark Sutherns to discuss all the latest at their clubs and the best Fantasy assets within them ahead of their GW17 meeting at Old Trafford.
 With all of United's first choice back four making the World Cup Quarter Finals is it now looking best to avoid United defensive assets? Is Marcus Rashford the obvious go to or would another United attacker be the best choice?
 Will Neco Williams maintain interest from FPL managers or is there too much of a rotation risk? Is Morgan Gibbs-White the go-to Forest attacker to consider for an enticing run after their trip to United? And would Dean Henderson be a better goalkeeper choice than David De Gea despite GW17 ineligibility?:
 Plus there's discussion on the managers and their respective starts to their debut Premier League seasons and the Podcast begins with a discussion on Cristiano Ronaldo's departure from United... 
 On Thursday: Planet SkyFF s4 ep19: A final discussion on Sky Fantasy assets for the Overhaul
 And on Patreon today it's Money In Football: "FIFA's Greed", discussion on FIFA's proposals for a 48 team World Cup and a Club World Cup
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? On Planet FPL Patreon, December is FREE for existing Patrons! And in January all Patrons will be boosted to the next tier level.
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 #FPL #MUFC #NFFC
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
