    <item>
      <title>Liverpool v Southampton | CotC with @FPL_LocoLord &amp; @CS_Wipeout | Planet FPL 2022/23</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/liverpool-v-southampton-cotc-with-fpl_locolord-cs_wipeout-planet-fpl-202223</link>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents this week James is joined by Liverpool fan Dan Lord and Southampton fan Matt Samuel to discuss all the latest at their clubs and preview Saturday's meeting at Anfield.
 Are Liverpool for sale? FSG are reported to be willing to negotiate on offers for control of the club. There’s discussion on if they’ve been good for Liverpool and whether The Reds can sustain challenging the likes of Manchester City in the longer term without added investment.
 And what now for Southampton? Ralph Hassenhuttl was dismissed on Monday with news at the time of recording suggesting Luton Town manager Nathan Jones will be next. There’s reflection on Hassenhuttl’s tenure and whether Jones is suitable replacement.
 Plus, FPL assets discussed with Liverpool players likely to be popular heading into the weekend meeting and both clubs have not only attractive, but also similar, fixtures after the World Cup.
 Follow Dan on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPL_LocoLord
 Follow Matt on Twitter: https://twitter.com/CS_Wipeout
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL – England’s World Cup Squad: Reaction to Gareth Southgate’s 26 man squad announcement
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Join Planet FPL Patreon in November and receive December free of charge! Today's Podcast is Tot&amp;Ham and features discussion on last night’s Carabao Cup ties
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 #Liverpool #Southampton #FPL
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
