    <item>
      <title>Everton v Leicester | CotC with @spirit_blues &amp; @AaronLagor | Planet FPL 2022/23</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/everton-v-leicester-cotc-with-spirit_blues-aaronlagor-planet-fpl-202223</link>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents this week James is joined by Everton fan Sean Norton and Leicester fan Aaron Lagor to discuss all the latest at their clubs and preview Saturday's evening kick off at Goodison Park.
 Back to back clean sheets for The Toffees will have FPL managers interested in the likes of Jordan Pickford, Conor Coady and a returning Nathan Patterson but with Leicester and Bournemouth up next could Dominic Calvert-Lewin also be worth investing in?
 Leicester have improved dramatically since the introduction of Wout Faes, are they now no longer a team to target? Could James Maddison be worth bringing back into FPL teams for trips to Everton and West Ham? And has Aaron changed his stance on Brendan Rodgers having survived what looked near certain dismissal earlier in the campaign?
 Plus, is Jamie Vardy's time coming to an end, 'Alex Iwobinho', the battle to stay up and lots more...  
 Follow Sean on Twitter: https://twitter.com/spirit_blues
 Follow Aaron on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AaronLagor
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - Ask James live stream scheduled for 3pm BST on the Planet FPL YouTube channel with a Podcast version to follow shortly after conclusion.
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Join Planet FPL Patreon in November and receive December free of charge! Today's Podcast is Tot&amp;Ham and features discussion on Tottenham's dramatic Champions League win in Marseille
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 #Everton #Leicester #FPL
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
