    <item>
      <title>If You Weren't So Kamikaze | Planet SkyFF S. 4 Ep. 11 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/if-you-werent-so-kamikaze-planet-skyff-s-4-ep-11-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>It's a big period in Sky Fantasy with a (nearly) full midweek programme next week and despite no fixture and despite the postponement of Arsenal's fixture with Manchester City assets from both clubs still appeal going into the weekend.
 There's discussion on upcoming captaincy for the next 6 days including Friday's Brenford v Brighton single gameday, why Harry Kane will be popular Saturday and if Erling Haaland should be opposed on Sunday. While all 3 midweek gamedays don't have obvious captaincy conclusions and Sky managers may have to prepare for Plan B
 Plus, binning Neco Williams now looks a priority for many, enabler options, key pointers from the weekend games, community questions answered and lots more...
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - Clash of the Correspondents: Southampton v West Ham with @CS_Wipeout &amp; @Fpl_SkyAddict
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in October features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier and today's Podcast offering is Tot&amp;Ham.
