    <item>
      <title>Liverpool v Brighton | CotC with @FPL_LocoLord &amp; @FPLSeagull | Planet FPL 2022/23</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/liverpool-v-brighton-cotc-with-fpl_locolord-fplseagull-planet-fpl-202223</link>
      <description>On Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Liverpool fan Dan Lord and Brighton fan Sam Murray to discuss a very eventful start to the season for their clubs and preview the Gameweek 9 meeting between the two clubs at Anfield.
 What's wrong with Liverpool? Results and performances have underwhelmed so far this season and a number of star performers have not been at their best. There's discussion on why The Reds have been short of their high standards.
 And it's all change for Brighton with Graham Potter moving to Chelsea and the appointment of Roberto De Zerbi. There's reflection on Potter's spell at The Seagulls, why it's so difficult for clubs like Brighton to break into the top 6 and an introduction to De Zerbi, who may bring a tactical style unlike anything we've seen before in the Premier League.
 Plus, what should FPL managers do now with their Brighton assets, if those who have gone without the likes of Trent Alexander-Arnold and Mo Salah should quickly get them in, or if it's viable, remarkably, to consider having no Liverpool assets at all... 
 Follow Dan on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPL_LocoLord
 Follow Sam on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPLSeagull
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - Ask James, scheduled for 4pm BST
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in September features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier and today's content features a Quiz on World Cup records.
