      <itunes:summary>Ahead of Friday's Gameweek 8 meeting between Nottingham Forest and Fulham James is joined by Cottagers Correspondent Dara Curran to discuss Fulham's start to the season and hopes ahead of a very attractive fixture run.
 There's discussion on Fulham's likely best starting eleven going forward with the squad firmed up by the additions of late transfer window signings Layvin Kurzawa, Daniel James and Willian but there have been some impressive performances from the likes of Tim Ream and Neeskens Kebano which mean there's no guarantee the new additions get straight into the team.
 Plus, early impressions on the integration of Bernd Leno, Paulinha and Andreas Pereira and why for FPL managers both Pereira and star striker Aleksander Mitrovic are so hard to ignore. But with the promising fixture run until the World Cup should a third Fulham asset be considered...? 
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - James's Final Wildcard Draft
