    <item>
      <title>Planning For The Unknown | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 13 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/planning-for-the-unknown-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-13-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>With no games to review following the sad passing of Queen Elizabeth II last Thursday and the postponement of the Premier League's Gameweek 7 Suj &amp; James discuss what may happen next as Gameweek 8 reamins in doubt.
 Could we lose the whole Gameweek again this coming weekend? What fixtures are most in danger?
 James details why he is in effect on Wildcard and why irrespective of what Gameweek 8 looks like it's the right play for him and Suj details why Wildcarding isn't necessary for him.
 There's a reminder for those considering a Free Hit in the event of a partial gameweek that it may be better deployed later in the season and there's also detail of when Gameweek 7 could be played and there is one scenario where it 'could' happen prior to the World Cup.
 Plus, many Twitter questions covered and why if there's a time to take on popular Arsenal and Liverpool assets it could be now...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - A Chelsea Special: @Phantomantle joins James to discuss the sacking of Thomas Tuchel and the appointment of Graham Potter
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
 ___________________________________________
