    <item>
      <title>Utterly Absurd | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 12 with @UtterlyTC | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/utterly-absurd-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-12-with-utterlytc-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Tom Campbell aka @UtterlyTC stands in again for Suj to join James and discuss the implications and fallout from a controversial Gameweek 6 in the Premier League - and leads to probably (we can't be bothered to research it) the longest Planet #FPL Podcast to date.
 There's debate on the VAR decisions that upset many football purists over the weekend and it was a difficult weekend for many FPL managers and it seems many Wildcards could be activated but James makes the case to wait a week.
 Among the controversy there was some very good football to discuss as Liverpool and Man City both slipped up and showed vulnerabilities, there's theory as to why both happened. Arsenal's 100% record went at Old Trafford but they played well for the majority while Tottenham took advantage with a much improved performance against Fulham. 
 Plus, Ivan Toney's hat-trick, Thomas Tuchel's interesting use of Raheem Sterling late in Chelsea's win, the tactical change that enabled a stunning comeback for Bournemouth and brilliant Brighton have left Brendan Rodgers on the brink...
 Follow Tom on Twitter: https://twitter.com/UtterlyTC
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - Clash of the Correspondents: Leicester City vs Aston Villa @AaronLagor &amp; @Lee_Jackson_92
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in September features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier and today's offering is The Patreon Q&amp;A
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 #FPL #FantasyPremierLeague #GW6Review
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
