      <itunes:subtitle>Ahead of today's Gameweek 5 deadline James is joined on a bonus Clash of the Correspondents by Bournemouth fan Neil Grover and Wolves fan Bradley Parker to discuss all the latest at their clubs and the FPL assets that may be of interest from them...</itunes:subtitle>
      <itunes:summary>Ahead of today's Gameweek 5 deadline James is joined on a bonus Clash of the Correspondents by Bournemouth fan Neil Grover and Wolves fan Bradley Parker to discuss all the latest at their clubs and the FPL assets that may be of interest from them ahead of their Wednesday night meeting on the South Coast.
 How does it feel to lose 9-0? There's reflection on Saturday's mauling at Anfield and if already Bournemouth look short of their 19 counterparts in the league? But could comfort come from an attractive upcoming set of fixtures that sees them meet only one of the Big 6 between now and the World Cup? 
 Currently there are 3 teams worse off than Bournemouth, one of which is opponents Wolves who come into this week without a win despite some reasonable performances. But with difficult fixtures coming up from GW7 the pressure is on to get results from the next 2 and scoring goals remains and ongoing issue.
 Plus, both managers could already be under pressure, could changes be made? And the interesting FPL enablers from both clubs including the fit again Dominic Solanke and pre-season fancied Pedro Neto get coverage...
 Follow Neil on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AFCBNG
 Follow Bradley on Twitter: https://twitter.com/parker_bradley
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - Planet SkyFF s4 ep5, as @ffscout_luke joins James for the Sky Fantasy Podcast. And still to come today James presents the GW5 Deadline Stream Live at 5pm BST on the Planet FPL YouTube channel.
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
