      <title>Peri Hot ITK | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 9 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/peri-hot-itk-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-9-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James review all the weekend games from Gameweek 3 in the Premier League and the fallout and impact on FPL.
 Early discussion focuses on James making an admittance about No Salah due to the form, or rather concerns around Heung-Min Son and why Thursday's Champions League draw could hold the key to several decisions for FPL managers in the coming weeks.
 Plus, Iavn Perisic is brilliant, Brendan Rodgers reign at Leicester feels like it's coming to an inevitable conclusion, Newcastle and Man City's 3-3 draw thrilled, Leeds pressed Chelsea into submission and Arsenal hold the only 100% record in the league after winning at Bournemouth, but for Suj's West Ham it's no points and no goals scored...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - The People's Poll Podcast, vote for your favourite via this tweet before 630pm BST  https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1559095197522345984?s=20&amp;t=Scdgmqxuo0W29HI5mlip4g
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
