      <title>Good Game | Planet FPL S. 6 Ep. 7 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/good-game-planet-fpl-s-6-ep-7-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James review the opening Gameweek of the Premier League season and discuss the latest things for their FPL teams where they both went No Salah but already have Erling Haaland on board.
 On the Pod: Why Arsenal seem to be better at 0-0, praise for Fulham, Bournemouth and Brighton for excellent weekend performances, the potential impact of Darwin Nunez on Liverpool, the brilliance of Dejan Kulusevski, Everton concern deepens with injuries, Ten Hag's debut to forget and Erling Haaland showed why the hype is real.
 Plus advice on not overreacting to one Gameweek and why many popular chosen assets who blanked may well be worth a second week
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - The People's Poll Podcast, vote for your favourite via this tweet before 530pm BST  https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1556543267952594944?s=20&amp;t=j2g3IWIZ62QRsWZXkHSieQ
