    <item>
      <title>Crystal Palace with @Migtavius | Correspondent Week ep 20 | Planet FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/crystal-palace-with-migtavius-correspondent-week-ep-20-planet-fpl-0</link>
      <description>On the final Podcast of Correspondent Week Suj &amp; James welcome the always brilliant Migtavius to discuss Crystal Palace and The Eagles hopes for the season ahead.
 With a daunting set of opening fixtures finding the right Palace asset appears difficult but does that mean we should overlook talisman Wilfried Zaha and the cheap defensive assets. There's data to suggest that perhaps we shouldn't.
 Also Luke Plange's chances of minutes, who's likely to start as number 1, why it's likely to remain a back four (for now), the difficulty in replacing Conor Gallagher and why our psyche should potentially change to treat Palace with more respect...
 Follow Mig on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Migtavius
 And a big thank you to all of the Correspondents for their amazing insights this week!!!
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - Planet FPL s6 ep6: Correspondent Week round-up and learnings from the weekend friendlies
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
