      <itunes:summary>Super Sunday Correspondent Week kicks off with Everton fan Sean Norton joining Suj &amp; James to discuss The Toffees. But is there anything super about Everton as we ahead into the new season? A season of struggle could await again...
 There's discussion on Frank Lampard, the board and why August is more important for Everton than any other Premier League club as they attempt to reshape the squad.
 Plus, Nathan Patterson appeals for FPL managers as a defensive enabler and there could now be strength in depth at the back with James Tarkowski a welcome addition to what may start as a back three, and Anthony Gordon could also appeal to FPL managers after a breakthrough 21/22 season, but he may not be the ony midfield asset to keep your eye on...
 Follow Sean on Twitter: https://twitter.com/spirit_blues
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - The final Correspondent Week Podcast; Crystal Palace with @Migtavius
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
