    <item>
      <title>Bournemouth with @AFCBNG | Correspondent Week ep 18 | Planet FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/bournemouth-with-afcbng-correspondent-week-ep-18-planet-fpl-0</link>
      <description>Bournemouth fan Neil Grover joins Suj and James to conclude Correspondent Week Saturday to discuss why the narrative around The Cherries from outside the club is negative going into their return to the Premier League.
 A lack of signings has fans and neutrals worried and means that currently Scott Parker can't switch to a back five should he so wish to do so because he doesn't have enough defenders to do it! And the opening fixtures are not kind.
 But there is a brilliant and sustained run that begins in Gameweek 5 that FPL managers should take note of and players such as Mark Travers, Jack Rothwell, Phil Billing and talisman Dominic Solanke should all be watched closely.
 Plus, a consciousness of being self sustaining, planned infrastructure improvements, the benefits of a settled squad and why FPL managers without Erling Haaland should take note...
 Follow Neil on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AFCBNG
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - The final two Correspondent Week Podcasts; Everton with @spirit_blues &amp; Crystal Palace with @Migtavius
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
