    <item>
      <title>Brentford with @FPLDummyTom | Correspondent Week ep 6 | Planet FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/brentford-with-fpldummytom-correspondent-week-ep-6-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James wrap up Correspondent Week Tuesday by discussing Brentford with @FPLDummyTom and there should be plenty of interest for FPL managers with some well priced assets and a very interesting opening set of fixtures.
 Is David Raya the clear number one in goal or could new signing Thomas Strakosha take his place? There's a detailed debate on the goalkeeper situation followed by concern about injuries at centre-back, a position which has been bolstered by the addition of Ben Mee.
 Is record signing Keane Lewis-Potter likely to start or will fellow 5.5 FPL midfielder Yoanne Wissa keep his place?
 Plus Aaron Hickey's potential, why Bryan Mbeumo shouldn't be discounted, second season syndrome, the loss of Christian Eriksen and the potential gold in 4.5 Josh DaSilva and the consistently excellent Ivan Toney...
 Follow Tom on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPLDummyTom
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - Correspondent Week episodes 7, 8 &amp; 9; Fulham with @TheTinkerMen, Aston Villa @Lee_Jackson_92 &amp; Manchester City with @FPLPringle
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in July features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier. Today's content features Tot&amp;Ham
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
