    <item>
      <title>Southampton with @CS_Wipeout | Correspondent Week ep 2 | Planet FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/southampton-with-cs_wipeout-correspondent-week-ep-2-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>On the second Podcast of Correspondent week Suj &amp; James speak to Southampton fan Matt Samuel to find out about Saints likely system and their new incomings.
 Three at the back appears to be the way Ralph Hassenhuttl wants to go, could this lead to greater solidity at the back for Saints? But could it also lead to concerns about scoring at the other end?
 There's discussion on imminent new signing Sekou Mara, but why Saints probably still need another additional striker. 
 Are new signings Gavin Bazunu, Armel Bella-Kotchap, Romeo Lavia and Joe Aribo likely starters and can they be considered as FPL options?
 Plus, depth concerns at wing-back, likley GW1 line-up, the nasty opening fixture runs, whether Matt would consider captaining Harry Kane or Heung-Min Son against Saints in GW1 and the consistency of James Ward-Prowse with comparisons to other 6.5 FPL assets...
 Follow Matt on Twitter: https://twitter.com/CS_Wipeout
 Still to come today on Planet FPL - Correspondent Week episode 3 on Nottingham Forest with @FFScout_Mark
 Join our Planet FPL Mini League: https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/yw6ree
 Patrons can find information on their mini leagues this season via this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/patreon-mini-69251447
 You can also join our Sky Fantasy Football Mini League. The Pin required is 8475785
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in July features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier. Today's content features the weekly Patreon Q&amp;A Podcast
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
