        <![CDATA[<p>Following on from yesterday's Podcast discussing the teams Suj &amp; James take a detailed look at the fixture schedule and agree that the promising schedule for last season's top 5 will lead towards an FPL template forming.</p> <p>There's a look at captaincy options in the opening gameweeks with comparison of when the premium FPL assets will be needed in our teams but there is difference of opinion in the studio.</p> <p>Plus, when might be a good time to Wildcard? Could swings around Gameweek 6 or 7 for the 'pretenders' offer a differential way of playing? </p> <p>And there's an overview of each team's good and bad spells... </p> <p>Tomorrow on Planet FPL - Planet FPL s6 ep3: An analysis of the known FPL prices</p> <p>___________________________________________</p> <p>Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in July features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier. Today's content features a discussion on the current state of Women's Football and a preview of the Women's Euros with Lauren Harris</p> <p>Join us on Patreon: <a href="https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl">https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl</a> </p> <p>Follow James on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod">https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod</a></p> <p>Follow Suj on Twitter: <a href="https://twitter.com/sujanshah">https://twitter.com/sujanshah</a></p> <p>Like us on Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl">https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Follow us on Instagram: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl">https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl</a></p> <p>Subscribe to our YouTube channel: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC8043oOKTB4uP8Nq15Kz6bg">https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC8043oOKTB4uP8Nq15Kz6bg</a></p><p> </p><p>Learn more about your ad choices. Visit <a href="https://podcastchoices.com/adchoices">podcastchoices.com/adchoices</a></p>]]>
