    <item>
      <title>Introducing Bournemouth (again) with @AFCBNG | Planet FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/introducing-bournemouth-again-with-afcbng-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>Bournemouth are back in the Premier League and following last week's crucial victory against promotion challenging Nottingham Forest James welcome Bournemouth correspondent Neil Grover back to the Podcast to discuss The Cherries promotion and what we can expect from them next season.
 There's discussion on 'Parker Ball' - is it boring? We find out there's strength in defence but it may be a weakness in the Prem, an overview of the squad, why Dominic Solanke's brilliant season has gone under the radar and if he's ready for the step up.
 Plus, why this promotion feels very different to Bournemouth's first...
 Follow Neil on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AFCBNG
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - Suj rejoins James for Planet FPL s5 ep53, reviewing all of the Gameweek 36 midweek games
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in May features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier. Today's content features Tot&amp;Ham with all the latest on Tottenham and West Ham including a look ahead to tonight's crucial North London Derby
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl 
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
 Follow us on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/planetfpl
 Subscribe to our YouTube channel: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC8043oOKTB4uP8Nq15Kz6bg
 #FPL #FantasyPremierLeague #Bournemouth
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
