    <item>
      <title>Wrong Bruno | Planet #FPL S. 5 Ep. 48 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/wrong-bruno-planet-fpl-s-5-ep-48-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj and James discuss the 6 weekend games so far in Gameweek 33 which saw many popular FPL assets underwhelm but Cristiano Ronaldo scored another hat-trick to reward many Free Hitters and Bruno did well too, just for James it was the wrong one.
 There's discussion on the next double ahead for Chelsea and Manchester United now that their rearranged fixture is confirmed for Gameweek 34, but is it that attractive?
 Plus...
 How bad were Tottenham on Saturday? Should there be concern for owners of their assets ahead of the trip to Brentford on Saturday?
 Can Arsenal or United catch them in the race for 4th?
 Wout Weghorst finally returned, but did Burnley in the absence of Sean Dyche impress?
 And variance, the continuing concern around rotation of Leicester assets and more...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - The People's Poll Podcast: Vote for your choice of topic before 430pm BST today via the Twitter post below  https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1515974259281125378?s=20&amp;t=7NY3htuRU5hkSnS632DgxQ
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in April features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier. Today's content features a Patreon exclusive Ask James Live Stream
