    <item>
      <title>Essential? Dispensable? | Planet SkyFF S. 3 Ep. 36 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/essential-dispensable-planet-skyff-s-3-ep-36-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>On this week's Sky Fantasy Football Podcast Suj and James and discuss transfers in mind ahead of potential re-entry points for the Premier League's Big 3 next midweek.
 There's discussion on the impact of Chelsea's Champions League exit and where the fixture with Manchester United may fall should Chelsea win their FA Cup semi final against Crystal Palace on Sunday and why what day Liverpool play in a possible Champions League semi final 1st leg could be critical for when to attack assets from The Reds.
 Plus, a rundown of best captaincy options for the week ahead including Kane vs Son for Saturday and there's coverage of the Twitter questions including talk of which block defence would be best and there's advice to keep an eye on Southampton...
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - Clash of the Correspondents: Burnley v Southampton with @TurfyTopper and CS_Wipeout
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in April features over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier. Today's Podcast is Tot&amp;Ham: Discussing all the latest on Tottenham and West Ham
