      <title>Utterly Brilliant | Planet #FPL S. 5 Ep. 45 with guest host @UtterlyTC | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/utterly-brilliant-planet-fpl-s-5-ep-45-with-guest-host-utterlytc-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>With Suj on holiday Tom Campbell steps in to Suj's shoes to host the Podcast and what follows is unplanned discussion on a range of football and FPL topics.
 There's discussion on future chips usage for the remaining gameweeks, being blinded by double gameweeks, player value impacting templates, goal setting, Manchester City differentials, GW31 captaincy and there's thoughts on the top 4 race, Arsenal, Manchester United and Tottenham, how Gareth Southgate has evolved the culture around the England national team, how much weight we should give stats into our thinking and the future of FPL content.
 Tomorrow on Planet FPL - Clash of the Correspondents: Burnley v Everton with @TurfyTopper and @spirit_Blues
 ____________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL community? Support our content on Patreon. March will feature over 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier and this week features 10 Audiobook episodes, Goodbye To The Lane, James's story of the 2016-17 season, Tottenham's last at the Old White Hart Lane
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl 
