    <item>
      <title>Tottenham v Newcastle | CotC with @Rickysaunders77 and @fpl_fitballer | Planet FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/tottenham-v-newcastle-cotc-with-rickysaunders77-and-fpl_fitballer-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>On this week's Planet FPL Clash of the Correspondents Podcast James is joined by Tottenham fan Ricky Saunders and Newcastle fan Simon Bibby to discuss all the latest at their clubs, and the all important FPL assets within them ahead of their Gameweek 31 meeting at White Hart Lane.
 Can Tottenham maintain their challenge for a top four finish after impressive victories against Brighton and West Ham?
 Can Newcastle make a late challenge for a top half finish with their top flight status now looking secure?
 And there's discussion on the FPL assets that matter including the possibility of going treble Tottenham offence with Dejan Kulusevski added to Heung-Min Son and Harry Kane, though for many it'll have to be just the one of Son or Kane. Which Tottenham defensive asset is best or should they be avoided?
 And Newcastle have a very attractive Double Gameweek 33 upcoming and there's certainly a case of trebling up for those on a Free Hit that week. But which three would it be best to get...?
 Follow Ricky on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Rickysaunders77
 Follow Si on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fpl_fitballer
 Coming Up on Friday on Planet FPL - Ask James at 1pm GMT on YouTube with an audio version to follow shortly afterwards
 ___________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL and SkyFF community and support the Podcast? Our Patreon content in February features 20 additional Podcasts from Intermediate Tier.
 Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl 
