    <item>
      <title>Offend Them | Planet #FPL S. 5 Ep. 44 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/offend-them-planet-fpl-s-5-ep-44-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj and James review the football from Blank Gameweek 30 with many template players missing out and even some that did start, (cough, cough, Raul Jimenez) frustrated many FPL managers. 
 Was the weekend a success for FPL managers who deployed the Free Hit? There was certainly some good scores among Free Hitters but also some fortune from the popular returnees too. 
 The 4 weekend games get the usual Monday overview and it includes extended discussion on Planet FPL derby success for James as Tottenham beat Suj's West Ham yesterday.
 James also outlines what Gameweeks 34 to 37 are likely to look like once games are rearranged, including which two teams could face back to back doubles and the complication around Chelsea's schedule. Plus why those intending to Free Hit in Gameweek 33 will be faced with difficult risk v reward decisions to make... 
 You can vote for your favourite topic for tomorrow's People's Poll Podcast via this tweet up until 5pm BST  https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1505831935578415105?s=20&amp;t=0L1T_4zUwqEu_ALDYU90DA
