    <item>
      <title>Creamy Pasta Boys | Planet #FPL S. 5 Ep. 42 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/creamy-pasta-boys-planet-fpl-s-5-ep-42-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James discuss all the football played during the Gameweek 29 weekend as Ronaldo's hat-trick dented Tottenham's Top 4 hopes and improves United's, Arsenal impressed again and VAR controversy overshadowed Chelsea's win over Newcastle.
 James details why he ended up taking a -12 this week and all eyes are focused towards the forthcoming Gameweek 30 that features only four fixtures with focused talk on those involved at the weekend including who it's dangerous to go without and those that appeal as one week punts.
 And what if Mo Salah is out for a while...?
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL the People's Poll Podcast, you can vote for your favourite via this tweet before 5pm BST   https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1503296195422298115?s=20&amp;t=pOXC4aKgR_IvnnRZFiLc3Q
 For our full schedule for the week view this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/63754215
