    <item>
      <title>Chelsea's Thirsty Thursday | Planet SkyFF S. 3 Ep. 31 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/chelseas-thirsty-thursday-planet-skyff-s-3-ep-31-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>On this week's Sky Fantasy Football Suj &amp; James discuss the race to buy Chelsea assets ahead of tomorrow night's trip to Norwich and how heavy Sky Fantasy managers should invest in The Blues.
 Or maybe they shouldn't? Is there a case with alternative captaincy options available on Thursday and Sunday to avoid The Blues completely and find gains later on? There's talk of the difficulty of moving from popular assets with the current crop of players owned by over 15% in the top one thousand all analysed to see if they can be sacrificed for Chelsea investment.
 Plus thoughts on captaincy for upcoming gamedays including why James is likely to back Conor Gallagher against Manchester City on Monday night, interest in Raphinha and awareness of the previously postponed fixture most likely to drop in after the international break. 
   Coming Up on Planet FPL tomorrow...  Clash of the Correspondents: Arsenal v Leicester City with @ThreeFiveWho &amp; @AaronLagor
 ____________________________________________
