    <item>
      <title>The Uprising | Planet #FPL S. 5 Ep. 40 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/the-uprising-planet-fpl-s-5-ep-40-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>On the review of the Gameweek 28 weekend Suj &amp; James discuss all the talking points from the 9 games played, including whether not buying Reece James was a regret, the punt that worked out for James and why both are considering making the same move ahead of Gameweek 29 though there could be a surprising second buy for James for a -4.
 There's discussion on players FPL managers may be considering subject to their strategy in the coming weeks, the Jarrod Bowen replacement that could be popular who hasn't played yet in this Gameweek, if those who haven't used the Triple Captaincy should this coming weekend and the importance of teams missing key central defenders...
 Coming up tomorrow on Planet FPL - The People's Poll Podcast, vote for your favourite via the tweet below before 5pm BST  https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1500758198583758852?s=20&amp;t=Sl2X4H_U72jm9h5S8fS-3g
 For our full schedule for the week view this post https://www.patreon.com/posts/63466725
