    <item>
      <title>We've All Been There | Planet SkyFF S. 3 Ep. 23 | Sky Fantasy Football</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/weve-all-been-there-planet-skyff-s-3-ep-23-sky-fantasy-football</link>
      <description>On this week's Sky Fantasy Football Suj &amp; James discuss thoughts on the remaining 9 gamedays between now and Overhaul and who they're likely to captain on each day.
 There's a review of the decision making ahead of last night's Southampton-Brentford encounter, what non owners should do for tonight's West Ham-Norwich and Friday's Brighton-Crystal Palace fixtures and when and why managers should consider buying Emmanuel Dennis or Josh King in advance of Watford hosting Norwich on Friday 21st.
 Plus there's a warning that there could be more fixtures to come, how that could impact the Overhaul period, why Sunday or Tuesday should be the end game for the majority of Sky managers and if Harry Kane should be considered ahead of the North London Derby...
 Coming Up on Planet FPL tomorrow...  Clash of the Correspondents: Aston Villa v Manchester United with @Lee_Jackson_92 &amp; @ismyCAPplaying
 ____________________________________________
