    <item>
      <title>Chip Talk | Planet #FPL S. 5 Ep. 29 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/chip-talk-planet-fpl-s-5-ep-29-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>With the FA Cup 3rd round dominating the weekend football Suj &amp; James discuss some of the talking points from the weekend, particularly in reference to their clubs Tottenham and West Ham and what it means for Double Gameweek 22 and the Podcast has a detailed focus on potential fixture rearrangements and Chip Strategy.
 To Free Hit or not Free Hit in Double Gameweek 22? There's discussion on the pros and cons and the assets to target ahead of Friday's deadline.
 James talks through future opportunities for the Free Hit later in the season including covering a potential Gameweek 27 problem and there's also a warning that one team could have a treble Gameweek as early as Gameweek 23!
 Plus, dealing with tomorrow's Everton-Leicester postponement, why the Premier League needs to look at it's Covid rules, captaincy for the weekend discussed and there's extended coverage of listeners questions...
 Coming Up on Tuesday on Planet FPL - The People's Poll Podcast, you can vote for your favourite from 3 options via this tweet until 6pm (UK) https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1480483311696982018?s=20
 ____________________________________________
