    <item>
      <title>Wolves v West Ham with @parker_bradley &amp; @Fpl_SkyAddict | Planet #FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/wolves-v-west-ham-with-parker_bradley-fpl_skyaddict-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>On this week's Planet FPL Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Wolves fan Bradley Parker and West Ham fan Chris Stone to discuss all the latest at their clubs, the FPL assets within them and preview next weekend's Gameweek 12 meeting at Molineux.
 Both clubs have been on good run so what are the realistic expectations for both for the remainder of the season? Can Wolves mount a challenge for European qualification and should a top 4 finish now be expected for The Hammers?
 Wolves good fixture run ends soon so should FPL managers be beginning to think of selling assets such as Raul Jimenez or is there a case, as James finds, that there is a case for still buying an asset for the gameweeks ahead?
 West Ham are already in the middle of a difficult fixture run, should their FPL assets be sold too or is there reason to hold stars such as Michail Antonio for the long-term?
 Follow Bradley on Twitter: https://twitter.com/parker_bradley
 Follow Chris on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Fpl_SkyAddict
 Coming Up on Friday on Planet FPL -Ask James, 3pm (UK) on YouTube with an audio version to follow shortly after conclusion of the stream
 ____________________________________________
