    <item>
      <title>Organised, But Harmless | Planet #FPL S. 5 Ep. 17 | Fantasy Premier League</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/organised-but-harmless-planet-fpl-s-5-ep-17-fantasy-premier-league</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James review all the games from Gameweek 11 games, a weekend that saw Chelsea slip up, Liverpool beaten and many FPL managers suffered benching horrors with too many good assets to choose from!
 There's discussion on the excellence of Conor Gallagher and Emile Smith-Rowe, why they'd both making it into a current wildcard team, Brentford assets failing to deliver, Man City's training victory and the big Tottenham debate continues with 4 attractive fixtures to come. Did we learn more from the goalless draw at Everton?
 ... Coming up on Tuesday, The People's Poll with Aston Villa correspondent @Lee_Jackson_90 discussing what next for Villa with Dean Smith dismissed.
