    <item>
      <title>Leeds V Leicester with @fpl_tactician &amp; @AaronLagor | Planet #FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/leeds-v-leicester-with-fpl_tactician-aaronlagor-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>On this week's Planet FPL Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Leeds fan Andy Martin and Leicester fan Aaron Lagor to discuss all the latest at their clubs, the FPL assets within them and preview Sunday's Gameweek 11 meeting at Elland Road.
 Are Leeds tired? They've underwhelmed so far this season and have been impacted by the loss of key players and some of them are still missing. Are they in for an unexpected battle against the drop?
 Leicester have also underwhelmed and their defensive record gives cause for concern. Can they push on and compete again for the European spots or is something not quite right with Brendan Rodgers current tactics?
 Plus, Kalvin Phillips' importance, why Harvey Branes and Kelechi Iheanacho influences Leicester's shape, the fascinating tactical battle, why Marcelo Bielsa will have to pick a flexible starting line up and it's agreed that this is not the week to back against Raphinha or Jamie Vardy returning...
 Follow Andy on Twitter: https://twitter.com/fpl_tactician
 Follow Aaron on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AaronLagor
 Coming Up on Friday on Planet FPL - The People's Poll Podcast, you can vote for whether the focus is on Newcastle, Norwich or Tottenham via this tweet until 530pm (UK) today https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod/status/1456208799006658561?s=20
 ____________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL community? Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
