    <item>
      <title>Tottenham v Aston Villa with @Rickysaunders77 &amp; @Lee_Jackson_92 | Planet #FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/tottenham-v-aston-villa-with-rickysaunders77-lee_jackson_92-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>On this week's Planet FPL Clash of the Correspondents James is joined by Tottenham fan Ricky Saunders and Aston Villa fan Lee Jackson to discuss their clubs, the FPL prospects from them and preview Sunday's meeting at White Hart Lane.
 It's three defeats in a row for Tottenham after Sunday's disastrous North London Derby defeat. Is this a full on crisis? Is Nuno's job under threat already? What does it all means for the prospects for Son and Kane in the coming weeks?
 While at Villa, a change of system to 3-5-2 has seen benefits, but is the switch here to stay? What does it mean for those both currently in and out of the team? And should we have our eyes on any of their FPL assets in the near future? 
 Follow Ricky on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Rickysaunders77
 Follow Lee on Twitter: https://twitter.com/Lee_Jackson_92
 Join our Planet FPL mini league, the winner will be invited on to a Planet FPL Podcast next summer! The code is d7mmxw or you can auto join at the link below https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/d7mmxw
 Coming Up on Friday on Planet FPL - Ask James, streaming live on YouTube at 3pm (UK) with an audio version to follow shortly afterwards
 ____________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL community? Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
 Follow James on Twitter: https://twitter.com/PlanetFPLPod
 Follow Suj on Twitter: https://twitter.com/sujanshah
 Like us on Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/planetfpl
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
