    <item>
      <title>Brighton v Leicester with @FPLSeagull &amp; Aaron Lagor | Planet #FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/brighton-v-leicester-with-fplseagull-aaron-lagor-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>James is joined by Brighton fan Sam Murray and Leicester fan Aaron Lagor on this week's Clash of the Correspondents to discuss their clubs and preview Sunday's Gameweek 5 meeting at The Amex.
 3 wins from the opening 4 for The Seagulls and have they now turned the tables on their xG critics from last season? Defensive options appeal particularly for FPL and has Adam Webster's injury now made Shane Duffy a lock in the short-term? And could we see Brighton revert to a back four in the coming weeks.
 Plus, something's not quite right at Leicester, the difficulty of fitting Harvey Barnes and Kelechi Iheanacho in the same team are discussed, James discusses his Ricardo Pereira frustrations and defenders returning from injury could lead to an upturn in results.
 Follow Sam on Twitter: https://twitter.com/FPLSeagull
 Follow Aaron on Twitter: https://twitter.com/AaronLagor
 Join our Planet FPL mini league, the winner will be invited on to a Planet FPL Podcast next summer! The code is d7mmxw or you can auto join at the link below https://fantasy.premierleague.com/leagues/auto-join/d7mmxw
 Coming Up on Friday on Planet FPL - Ask James, streaming live on YouTube at 3pm (UK) with an audio version to follow shortly afterwards
 ____________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL community? Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
