    <item>
      <title>Newcastle with @fpl_fitballer - Correspondent Week ep 3 | Planet #FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/newcastle-with-fpl_fitballer-correspondent-week-ep-3-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>Day 1 of Planet FPL's Correspondent Week concludes with Simon Bibby joining Suj &amp; James to discuss all things about Si's club Newcastle United.
 Is it a case of Callum Wilson or nothing from an FPL perspective? The case is made for Newcastle's talisman and a there's a warning that his consistency shouldn't neccessary be overlooked.
 There's frustration about the classification of some of the FPL assets but there could be some cheap enablers who appeal (The Sports Direct bench!), but there is an ongoing Goalkeeper crisis to be conscious of.
 And the proposed Takeover of the club will drag on until at least 2022 and Steve Bruce looks set to stay as manager. Si gives his opinion on why it's likely to be same old, same old for his club this season... but should we be taking more note of their brilliant and almost unnoticed end of season form...?
 You can follow Si on Twitter https://twitter.com/fpl_fitballer
 Coming up next on Correspondent Week - Burnley with @TurfyTopper
 ____________________________________________
 Want to become a member of our FPL community? Join us on Patreon: https://www.patreon.com/planetfpl
