      <description>In the first of two podcasts focusing on the home nations not called England who have qualified for the Euros Suj &amp; James welcome Ross Corfield to discuss all things Wales ahead of their Euro 2020 opener against Switzerland on Saturday.
 There's a discussion on the legacy and influence of Gary Speed, the amazing run to the semi finals of 2016, what's changed since, likely tactics and line-up for the Euros, expectancy, hopes, realism and why Ryan Giggs is technically still the manager but won't be with the squad this summer...
 You can follow Ross on Twitter @ CORF_FPL https://twitter.com/CORF_FPL
 James is also a guest on The FPL Happy Hour's 24th and final preview Podcast previewing England's hopes at The Euros https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PbZmw4WsLF0
 Our Euro 2020 mini league code is 64TZLYUG08 https://gaming.uefa.com/en/uefaeuro2020fantasyfootball/leagues/64TZLYUG08/0050006C0061006E00650074002000460050004C/James%20Linden
