      <description>The outrage is real, it appears no one is in favour of the new handball rules and incidents that cost Crystal Palace &amp; Tottenham over the weekend have intensified the anger. But is this an English problem? Have the rest of Europe already accepted these new interpretations of the law? We talk about injustice, right, wrong, solutions &amp; why we are part to blame for allowing the handball laws to be implemented. Plus, for Fantasy should we just stock our teams now with penalty takers?
