    <item>
      <title>A Spoonful Of Sugar | #ThrowbackThursday | Planet #FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/a-spoonful-of-sugar-throwbackthursday-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>On this Thursday Throwback Suj &amp; James look back on Alan Sugar's (Sir or Lord depending on your current preferences) period as Chairman of Tottenham Hotspur between 1991 and 2000. There's a focus on Sugar's takeover with Terry Venables and the court case that would lead to Venables departure from the club in 1993, plus a host of managerial mistakes during the 90s as the White Hart Lane club stood still while other clubs progressed. Yet there were still stars at The Lane to be remembered with fondness such as Teddy Sheringham, David Ginola &amp; there's insight into the incredible and shocking signing of Jurgen Klinsmann. James offers a fan account of his memories of Tottenham in the 90s and there are laughs aplenty at many of the mishaps that encountered the North London Club.
 ________________________________
