    <item>
      <title>#PremierLeagueSquadChallenge | The People's Poll Ep. 36 | Planet #FPL</title>
      <link>https://sites.libsyn.com/104154/premierleaguesquadchallenge-the-peoples-poll-ep-36-planet-fpl</link>
      <description>Suj &amp; James present the #PremierLeagueSquadChallenge
 Here's the Rules that James abided by in an attempt to pick his squad on this weeks People's Poll Podcast:
  Select a squad of 25 players
 Must be cover in every position (eg 2 left backs) &amp; must be 3 goalkeepers
 Players can only have played for 1 club in the Premier League
 No two players can be picked from the same Premier League club
 No two players can be picked from the same country
 A player must be picked from all of the current 20 Premier League clubs but doesn't have to be at that club now + from 5 previous Premier League clubs
 Each player must have a squad number between 1 &amp; 25 &amp; they must be assigned a number they wore for their club as a player
 
For example you could select David Beckham as he has only played in the Premier League for one club, but you could not pick another Englishman or Manchester United player. He could be assigned the squad number of 7 or 24

  ___________________________________________
 Web: www.planetfpl.com
 Twitter: @PlanetFPLPod (James) / @sujanshah (Suj)
 Facebook: www.facebook.com/PlanetFPL
 Instagram: @planetfpl
 You Tube: www.youtube.com/planetfpl
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices</description>
