      <description>On today's Ask James, discussion centred on life without football, the potential impacts on lower league clubs, why James is feeling positive that a rescue package may help smaller clubs survive, fears that football may not return for a long time &amp; why Man City's Champions League ban appeal may yet be a long way off.
 James also discusses the Tottenham asset that he feels may be financial expendable, there's an interruption from little Harry, managers we wouldn't want to fight and more...
